diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.examplenew file mode 100644index 0000000..a7c60a8--- /dev/null+++ b/.env.example@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@+# Root runner environment+# Used when starting the API from repo root with:+#   python run_api_server.py+#+# This repo currently has no committed `models/` directory.+# Create one yourself or point these paths somewhere else on disk.++AI_PROVIDER=huggingface++# OpenAI+OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key-here+OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4++# Cerebras+CEREBRAS_API_KEY=your-cerebras-api-key-here+CEREBRAS_MODEL=llama3.1-8b++# Baseten+BASETEN_API_KEY=your-baseten-api-key-here+BASETEN_MODEL_ID=your-baseten-model-id-here++# Hugging Face remote API+HF_API_KEY=your-huggingface-token-here+HF_MODEL=NousResearch/Hermes-3-Llama-3.1-8B+HF_BASE_URL=https://api-inference.huggingface.co/v1/++# Hugging Face local Transformers model+# Point to a folder that contains config/tokenizer/weights files.+# Example:+# HF_LOCAL_MODEL_PATH=models/llama3_8b_chat_uncensored+HF_LOCAL_MODEL_PATH=++# Ollama model name, served by your Ollama instance+OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1+OLLAMA_MODEL=hf.co/DavidAU/DeepSeek-MOE-4X8B-R1-Distill-Llama-3.1-Deep-Thinker-Uncensored-24B-GGUF++# llama.cpp local GGUF file+# Point to one GGUF file, not a directory.+# Example:+# LLAMA_CPP_MODEL_PATH=D:/models/OpenAi-GPT-oss-20b.gguf+LLAMA_CPP_MODEL_PATH=+LLAMA_CPP_N_CTX=2048+LLAMA_CPP_N_GPU_LAYERS=0+LLAMA_CPP_SEED=-1+LLAMA_CPP_VERBOSE=Falsediff --git a/.github/copilot-instructions.md b/.github/copilot-instructions.mdindex 8273346..16d0c91 100644--- a/.github/copilot-instructions.md+++ b/.github/copilot-instructions.md@@ -6,7 +6,21 @@ You are a perfume chemist assistant working with a hobbyist perfumer's inventory ## Critical Rules  ### 1. ALWAYS Read inventory.txt Before Formulating-NEVER rely on memory, session summaries, or assumptions about what materials are available. Read `inventory.txt` in full before writing any formula. Materials have specific dilutions (10%, 1%, 20%, 30%, 50%, 80%) that affect dosing โ€” you must account for these.+**This is RULE ZERO. Do not skip this step. Do not rely on memory. Do not assume stock availability.**++Read `inventory.txt` in full before writing any formula. Materials have specific dilutions (10%, 1%, 20%, 30%, 50%, 80%) that affect dosing โ€” you must account for these. Inventory changes between sessions โ€” what was available last week may be depleted today.++### 1b. ALL Calculations Must Use ppm, ODT, and OAV+**This is RULE 1. No exceptions. It applies to formulation, dosing, gating, scoring, and all pipeline modules.**++- **Concentrations** are in **ppm** (parts per million w/w in concentrate). Every material dose must be convertible to ppm.+- **Odor Detection Thresholds** are in **ODT** โ€” ppm for ethanol solution, ppb for air. Every threshold check must reference ODT.+- **Odor Activity Value** is **OAV = concentration_ppm / ODT_ppm**. Every perceptibility claim must be backed by OAV.+- Materials with OAV < 1 are below threshold and should not be counted as perceptible.+- Materials with OAV 1โ€“5 are perceptible but weak.+- Materials with OAV 5โ€“50 are clearly perceptible.+- Materials with OAV > 50 are dominant and may need reduction.+- Use `engine/perception/oav.py` for OAV computation. Use `engine/odor_thresholds.py` for ODT lookups.  ### 2. Use Perfumer Vocabulary, Not Fragrance-Fan Language Think in **chemical effects**, not vibes:@@ -213,6 +227,26 @@ The inventory has **3 key fixative-diffusion materials**. They are NOT interchan - Don't ignore the specialty materials (DBCA, Paradisamide, Scentenal, Cyclamen Aldehyde, Dynascone, etc.) - Don't add decorative ingredients at trace levels that won't contribute to the scent +### 16. Never Change the Fragrance Family When Modifying or Optimizing+When asked to optimize, enhance, or add "luxury/sparkle/glamour" to an existing formula, the fragrance family is a **hard boundary**. A woody chypre stays a woody chypre. A fougรจre stays a fougรจre. An oriental stays an oriental.++**Family-shifting materials to watch (these change genre when overdosed):**+| Material | Family it shifts toward | Safe ceiling in non-oriental contexts |+|----------|------------------------|---------------------------------------|+| Benzoin Resinoid | Oriental-balsamic | 30 ยตL of 50% per 6 mL concentrate |+| Labdanum Absolute | Oriental-amber | 20 ยตL of 10% per 6 mL concentrate |+| Coumarin | Fougรจre-oriental | 25 ยตL of 20% per 6 mL concentrate |+| Vanillin / Ethyl Vanillin | Gourmand-oriental | 30 ยตL neat per 6 mL concentrate |+| Heliotropin / Heliotropal | Powdery-oriental | 15 ยตL neat per 6 mL concentrate |+| Cashmeran | Oriental-woody | 50 ยตL neat per 6 mL concentrate |+| Cinnamaldehyde / Eugenol | Spice-oriental | 10 ยตL neat per 6 mL concentrate |++**Verification checklist before finalizing any formula modification:**+1. State the original family explicitly+2. Check every new or boosted material against the family-shifting table above+3. If the total of family-shifting materials exceeds ceilings, the family has drifted โ€” scale back+4. The incense/transparent/woody spine must dominate the base in non-oriental contexts+ ## File Locations - **Inventory:** `inventory.txt` โ€” MUST read before every formula - **Formulas:** `luxury_formulas_2026-03-26.md` โ€” established format referencediff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..b24655d--- /dev/null+++ b/AGENTS.md@@ -0,0 +1,183 @@+# AGENTS.md โ€” Perfume Chemistry++> **โ ๏ธ RULE 0: Read [`inventory.txt`](/inventory.txt) before constructing ANY fragrance.**  +> Materials, dilutions, and stock levels change. Never assume availability. Never rely on memory. Verify every material against the live inventory before dosing. This applies to all agents, all sessions, all formulas โ€” no exceptions.++> **โ ๏ธ RULE 1: All perfume calculations must use ppm, ODT, and OAV.**  +> Concentrations are in **ppm** (parts per million w/w in concentrate). Odor detection thresholds are **ODT** (in ppm for ethanol solution, or ppb for air). Odor Activity Value is **OAV = concentration_ppm / ODT_ppm**. Every formula dose must be convertible to ppm, every threshold check must reference ODT, and every perceptibility claim must be backed by OAV. No exceptions โ€” this applies to formulation, dosing, gating, scoring, and all pipeline modules.++## Repo architecture++Two separate Python environments โ€” they don't share a package manager:++| Scope | Entry | Package manager | Location |+|-------|-------|-----------------|----------|+| `engine/` (+ root scripts & pipelines) | `import engine.xxx` | pip `requirements.txt` | repo root |+| `backend/` FastAPI app | `import app.xxx` | Poetry | `backend/` |++`engine/` is a namespace package (no `__init__.py`). Root scripts and pipelines register the workspace root on `sys.path` to resolve `engine.xxx` imports. `backend/` is an independent Poetry project that does **not** depend on `engine/` โ€” they run in separate processes.++## Commands++### Backend (FastAPI)+```bash+cd backend+poetry install+poetry run ruff check app              # lint+poetry run mypy app --ignore-missing-imports   # typecheck+poetry run pytest --cov=app --cov-report=term  # test (needs OPENAI_API_KEY=test-key)+poetry run uvicorn app.main:app --reload       # dev server+```++### Engine + root tests+```bash+pip install -r requirements.txt+pytest tests/                          # from repo root (conftest adjusts sys.path)+```++### Run the API from root+```bash+python run_api_server.py               # manually sets up sys.path, then runs uvicorn+```+Or via Docker: `docker compose up -d`++### Run a single test+```bash+cd backend && poetry run pytest tests/unit/test_xxx.py -k test_name+```+```bash+pytest tests/test_pipeline_gates.py -k test_gate_blocks+```++## CI order (important)++From `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: `ruff check app` โ’ `mypy app --ignore-missing-imports` โ’ `pytest --cov=app`. Same order applies locally.++## Key conventions++- **Always read `inventory.txt` before formulating.** The `.github/copilot-instructions.md` contains extensive rules for perfume formulation, material selection, and dosing. Agents creating formulas **must** read it.+- **Two test directories**: `tests/` (engine-level tests, runs from root) and `backend/tests/` (API tests, runs via Poetry). Each has its own `conftest.py` with different `sys.path` and fixture setups.+- **Test env vars**: `OPENAI_API_KEY=test-key`, `SECRET_KEY=test-secret-key-for-ci`, and `PERFUME_PIPELINE_AUDIT_PATH` (auto-set by root `conftest.py` to a tempfile).+- **`inventory.txt` format**: `--- CATEGORY ---` headers, `- Material Name (dilution%)` bullets. Parsed by `engine/inventory_parser.py` which deduplicates by keeping the highest-dilution entry.+- **`archive/` and `output/` are gitignored** โ€” scratch scripts (prefix `_`) and generated outputs go there.+- **Pipeline scripts** in `pipelines/` are depth-1 orchestrators that self-register the repo root on `sys.path` and import `engine/` modules directly.+- **`.vscode/`, `.claude/`, `*.db`, `*.xlsx`, `*.csv`, `*.png` are gitignored.**+- **`engine/` dependencies** (`sentence-transformers`, `faiss-cpu`, `torch`, etc.) are in root `requirements.txt`, not in the Poetry project.++## When formulating perfumes++The `.github/copilot-instructions.md` file has mandatory rules: no material defaults (evaluate every option), use perfumer vocabulary, justify every material choice, build 2โ€“3 material musk chords across depth/projection/character-echo axes, and always read `inventory.txt` first. Agents generating formulas should treat that file as a required reference.++---++## Data Pipeline Architecture++### Data flow++```+ODT_DATA (odor_thresholds.py) โ”€โ”€โ’ ingredient_intelligence._PROFILES โ”€โ”€โ’ _generate_material_properties.py โ”€โ”€โ’ material_properties.json+        โ• (enrich at import)              โ• (alias resolution)                                 โ‘+   ODT_VERIFICATION                  name_utils._ALIASES                                         โ”โ”€ CAS_MAP (generator)+                                                                                                 โ”โ”€ TYPICAL_DOSE (generator)+                                                                                                 โ””โ”€ PubChem live API (generator)+```++Three separate data paths consume material properties:+1. **`material_properties.json`** โ€” used by scoring, OAV guards, and analysis scripts+2. **`ingredient_intelligence._PROFILES`** โ€” used directly by pipeline gates, formula_state, and direct profile lookups+3. **`ODT_DATA`** โ€” used by pipeline formula_state._lookup_odt(), ingredient_intelligence auto-populate++**Critical: These three paths are NOT automatically synchronized.** Changes to one often leave stale values in another. Run `python _generate_material_properties.py` to resync.++### `material_properties.json` coverage (verified 2026-05-11)++| Field | Coverage |+|---|---|+| MW, VP, cLogP | 210/210 (100%) |+| ODT air, ODT ethanol | 210/210 (100%) |+| OAV typical | 210/210 (100%) |+| Smell strength, anosmic risk | 210/210 (100%) |+| Note, role, activity_coef | 210/210 (100%) |+| Odor family | 209/210 (99%) |+| Texture, synergies | 204/210 (97%) |+| Hedonic | 161/210 (77%) |+| IFRA Cat4 limit | 87/210 (41% โ€” expected, not all restricted) |+| Hill EC50 | 25/210 (12%) |++## Known Data Quality Issues++### 1. ODT_VERIFICATION vs ODT_DATA duplication+`odor_thresholds.py` has TWO dicts โ€” `ODT_DATA` (numeric values) and `ODT_VERIFICATION` (metadata only). Both contain entries for the same materials. **Numeric ODT values must exist in BOTH** โ€” the last entry wins in `ODT_DATA`, so `ODT_VERIFICATION` entries that appear later in the file do NOT affect lookups. However, `_lookup_odt()` only reads `ODT_DATA`.++### 2. Hedione/Hedione HC ODT collision+`engine/name_utils.py` aliases `"hedione hc" โ’ "hedione"`. This causes `ODT_DATA` keys for both to normalize to the same name, and the later entry (`hedione hc` with `odt_air=20.0`) overwrites the earlier (`hedione` with `odt_air=0.05`). The peer-reviewed pure-isomer ODT (0.05 ppb) is therefore inaccessible for the formula_state pipeline. The practical value (20.0 ppb) is used for both.++### 3. Non-inventory legacy entries+`material_properties.json` contains entries with `"in_inventory": false` โ€” materials that existed in the knowledge graph but are no longer in `inventory.txt`. These were previously copied as-is without validation. The generator now force-overrides their physical properties (MW, VP, cLogP, ODT) from `_PROFILES` on regeneration.++### 4. Name normalization inconsistencies+`inventory_parser._canonical_name()` strips trailing parentheticals (e.g., `"Rosemary EO (French...)"` โ’ `"Rosemary EO"`), but `normalize_name()` in `name_utils.py` preserves them. The generator ALIASES dict bridges this gap, but must be kept in sync with inventory additions. The non-inventory enrichment loop also uses ALIASES for alias resolution.++### 5. `_generate_material_properties.py` is NOT import-safe+Running `import _generate_material_properties` executes the full generation pipeline at module level. Import for function access will trigger a full regenerate + PubChem API calls. The ALIASES and CAS_MAP dicts are defined at module scope and cannot be imported separately without side effects.++## Scientific Constraints (codified from system reference docs)++### Headspace OAV calculation+```+p_i = ฮณ_i ร— x_i ร— P_i*   (Modified Raoult)+OAV = p_i / P_atm ร— 1e6 / ODT_ppb+```+- `x_i` = mole fraction (must convert from weight via `n_i = w_i / MW_i`)+- `P_i*` = pure-component VP (Pa at 25ยฐC)+- `ฮณ_i` = activity coefficient in ethanol matrix (NEVER silently 1.0)++### Activity coefficient ranges (ethanol matrix, ~20ยฐC)+| Class | ฮณ |+|---|---|+| Non-polar hydrocarbons (limonene, pinenes, terpenes) | 3.0โ€“3.2 |+| Polar esters (benzyl acetate, linalyl acetate) | 1.5โ€“2.0 |+| Mid-polarity sesquiterpenes/alcohols | 1.2โ€“1.8 |+| H-bond donors/acceptors (vanillin, coumarin, musks) | 0.5โ€“0.7 |+| Macrocyclic musks | 0.4โ€“0.6 |++### Note tier from VP+| Tier | VP range |+|---|---|+| Top | > 50 Pa |+| Heart | 0.5โ€“50 Pa |+| Base | < 0.5 Pa |++### Psychophysics+- Weber-Fechner: `I = k ร— log(C / ODT)`+- Stevens Power Law: `I = k ร— C^n` (n typically 0.2โ€“0.6)+- OAV > 1 = perceptible. OAV < 0.1 = dormant filler.+- Humans can discriminate at most 3โ€“4 components in a mixture (Livermore & Laing)+- Adaptation: citrus adapts ~5 min, florals ~15โ€“20 min, musks ~45โ€“60 min++### Clausius-Clapeyron temperature correction+`ln(P2/P1) = (ฮ”Hvap/R) ร— (1/T1 - 1/T2)` where ฮ”Hvap โ 60 kJ/mol (working approximation). 10ยฐC rise โ’ VP ร— ~1.9. Bangkok (35ยฐC) vs Paris (22ยฐC): VP ร— ~2.8.++### EU Allergen labeling (Reg 1223/2009 Annex III)+26 mandatory allergens must be declared if exceeding 0.001% in leave-on or 0.010% in rinse-off products. SCCS Opinion SCCS/1525/21 proposes expansion to 82+ allergens as of 2026โ€“2027.++## Recent Changes (2026-05-11)++### Fixed: Benzoin Resinoid ODT in DHC V Formula+- ODT was 50.0 ppb (wrong), corrected to 3.0 ppb+- OAV recalculated from 0 to 5+- Material_properties.json physical properties corrected to match profile (VP=0.02 Pa, MW=212, cLogP=2.5)++### Fixed: ODT_DATA numeric values lost+32 materials had numeric `odt_air`/`odt_eth` values accidentally replaced by verification-only metadata in a previous edit. Restored from git HEAD with verification metadata preserved. Affected materials include: alpha-isomethyl ionone, alpha/beta ionone, hedione, iso e super, coumarin, vanillin, linalool, citronellol, geraniol, eugenol, indole, and others.++### Fixed: Generator force-override for non-inventory entries+`_generate_material_properties.py` now force-overrides physical properties (MW, VP, cLogP, note, role, texture, ODT) from profiles for ALL entries, including non-inventory legacy entries. Previously only filled NULL fields.++### Fixed: Missing profiles added+Added profiles to `ingredient_intelligence.py` for: Diethyl Phthalate, Dipropylene Glycol, Ethanol, Isopropyl Myristate, Triethyl Citrate, Lemon FCF oil Sicilian, Heliotropin, Molecule Iris. Added ODT entries for solvents (DEP, DPG, IPM, TEC).++### Fixed: Alias mapping errors+- `Cyclimal Aldehyde`: was aliased to `Florol` (wrong), corrected to `Cyclamen Aldehyde`+- Generator ALIASES: `amyl cinnamic aldehyde` โ’ `ACA`, `rosemary eo` โ’ `Rosemary EO (French Rosmarinus Officinalis leaf oil)`, `lemon fcf oil sicilian` โ’ `Lemon FCF oil Sicilian`+- Added aliases for legacy variants with parenthetical namesdiff --git a/DHC_CITRUS_SCORING.txt b/DHC_CITRUS_SCORING.txtnew file mode 100644index 0000000..770fa3b--- /dev/null+++ b/DHC_CITRUS_SCORING.txt@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@+==========================================================================================+  CITRUS-AWARE SCORING + HEDONISM+  Genre-adjusted for citrus colognes (transparency, freshness, radiance)+==========================================================================================++------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+  DHC A Lemon 100mL (fresh)+  14 materials | 12000 uL active | 12.0% v/v | 100 mL+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+  HEDONISM:        100.0/100  (pleasure/pleasantness index)+  CITRUS PURITY:    90.1/100  (how close to ideal citrus cologne)+  BAD OAV:           0.0%       (locked materials altering profile)+  CITRUS OAV:       75.1%     (of total headspace)+  CLEAN OAV:        68.8%     (modern/clean materials)+  PYRAMID:         75%T / 23%H / 2%B++  AXIS             SCORE+  --------------------  ------+  freshness             70.1  ##############------+  transparency          84.8  ################----+  radiance              85.3  #################---+  balance               93.1  ##################--+  longevity            100.0  ##########