cean LP | **Cobalt** |+|---|---|---|---|---|---|+| DHM | 200+ | ~100 | ~150 | ~120 | **100** |+| Ambrox | heavy | heavy | med | med | **heavy** |+| Sandalwood | none | creamy trio | light | trace | **trio** |+| Incense | none | trace | hint | none | **5 ยตL active** |+| Moss | none | none | none | none | **15 ยตL Evernyl** |+| Geraniol/rose | none | none | none | none | **100** |++Sprayed blind: registers as a blue family member. Side by side: identifiable as its own thing via the incense-moss depth and subtle rosy lift. Mall customer won't notice. Fragrance nerd will.diff --git a/formulas/Cobalt_Cedar_Air_30mL_EDP_Optimized.md b/formulas/Cobalt_Cedar_Air_30mL_EDP_Optimized.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..22a8b5b--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Cobalt_Cedar_Air_30mL_EDP_Optimized.md@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@+# Cobalt Cedar Air โ€” Optimized (Longevity + Projection + Smell, Cedar-First, No DHM Boost)++**Date:** 2026-05-03  +**Method:** constrained local-search optimizer with smell-preservation guardrail  (max drift 250 ยตL, step sizes 25 ยตL / 50 ยตL).+**DHM directive:** locked at original dose โ€” user saving DHM for sport cologne project.++## Guardrails++- Total concentrate locked at `5.920 mL`.+- No new materials introduced; original roster of 34 materials kept.+- Max drift from original: `250 ยตL` (~4.2 % of concentrate).+- Key character materials (Ambrox Super, Iso E Super, Sandalore, Ginger, Pink Pepper) protected by tight drift.++## Weighted Axes++| Axis | Weight | Maps to |+|---|---|---|+| longevity | 1.0 | MW + fixative load โ€” core target |+| projection (sillage) | 1.0 | VP + boosters โ€” core target |+| smell (hedonic) | 1.0 | intrinsic pleasantness โ€” core target |+| skin performance | 1.0 | reservoir kinetics โ€” longevity contributor |+| perceptual clarity | 0.5 | mixture suppression โ€” smell clarity |+| luxury | 0.3 | ingredient quality |+| texture | 0.3 | haptic / creamy / silky |+| depth (stacking) | 0.3 | structural layering |+| synergy | 0.2 | pairing-rule hits |+| photorealism | 0.2 | glass-like definition |++## Score Summary++**Geometric total:** `72.8` โ’ `74.1` (`+1.3`)++| Axis | Original | Optimized | Delta |+|---|---|---|---|+| longevity | 89.1 | 88.8 | -0.3 |+| sillage | 86.5 | 92.5 | +6.0 |+| luxury | 43.2 | 43.2 | +0.0 |+| texture | 82.8 | 83.0 | +0.2 |+| stacking_depth | 71.0 | 71.0 | +0.0 |+| hedonic | 83.5 | 83.9 | +0.4 |+| synergy | 95.0 | 95.0 | +0.0 |+| skin_performance | 45.9 | 47.4 | +1.5 |+| perceptual_clarity | 73.3 | 73.3 | +0.0 |+| photorealism | 79.6 | 79.9 | +0.3 |++**Main shifts:** Patchouli EO -0.100 mL; Beta-Pinene +0.075 mL; Norlimbanol Dextro -0.025 mL; Lime Distilled EO +0.025 mL; Geraniol +0.025 mL++## Optimized Formula++| Material | Original ยตL | Optimized ยตL | Delta ยตL |+|---|---:|---:|---:|+| Iso E Super | 850 | 850 | +0 |+| Ambrofix | 800 | 800 | +0 |+| Cedarwood Virginia | 400 | 400 | +0 |+| Cedrat FCF Sicilian | 380 | 380 | +0 |+| Galaxolide | 380 | 380 | +0 |+| Sandalore | 350 | 350 | +0 |+| Ethylene Brassylate | 230 | 230 | +0 |+| Habanolide | 220 | 220 | +0 |+| Ebanol | 210 | 210 | +0 |+| Hedione | 200 | 200 | +0 |+| Vetiver EO | 200 | 200 | +0 |+| Cashmeran | 200 | 200 | +0 |+| Benzoin Resinoid | 200 | 200 | +0 |+| Patchouli EO | 130 | 30 | -100 |+| Lime Distilled EO | 120 | 145 | +25 |+| Polysantol | 120 | 120 | +0 |+| Dihydromyrcenol | 100 | 100 | +0 |+| Lavender EO | 100 | 100 | +0 |+| Geraniol | 100 | 125 | +25 |+| Floralozone | 80 | 80 | +0 |+| Timberol | 80 | 80 | +0 |+| Azarbre | 80 | 80 | +0 |+| Coumarin | 60 | 60 | +0 |+| Linalyl Acetate | 50 | 50 | +0 |+| Norlimbanol Dextro | 50 | 25 | -25 |+| Olibanum Resinoid | 50 | 50 | +0 |+| Aldehyde C11 undecylenic | 40 | 40 | +0 |+| Methyl Pamplemousse | 30 | 30 | +0 |+| Hedione HC | 30 | 30 | +0 |+| Vertofix | 25 | 25 | +0 |+| Beta-Pinene | 15 | 90 | +75 |+| Evernyl | 15 | 15 | +0 |+| Nagarmotha Oil | 15 | 15 | +0 |+| Scentenal | 10 | 10 | +0 |+| **Ethanol 96 %** | **24080** | **24080** | **0** |++## Optimizer Moves++- Iter 1: shifted 0.050 mL from Cashmeran โ’ Beta-Pinene  (total 72.8 โ’ 73.6,  longevity 89.1 โ’ 89.0,  sillage 86.5 โ’ 91.2)+- Iter 2: shifted 0.050 mL from Patchouli EO โ’ Geraniol  (total 73.6 โ’ 73.9,  longevity 89.0 โ’ 88.9,  sillage 91.2 โ’ 92.2)+- Iter 3: shifted 0.025 mL from Ebanol โ’ Beta-Pinene  (total 73.9 โ’ 74.0,  longevity 88.9 โ’ 88.9,  sillage 92.2 โ’ 92.8)+- Iter 4: shifted 0.050 mL from Ethylene Brassylate โ’ Cashmeran  (total 74.0 โ’ 74.1,  longevity 88.9 โ’ 88.7,  sillage 92.8 โ’ 92.8)+- Iter 5: shifted 0.025 mL from Patchouli EO โ’ Ebanol  (total 74.1 โ’ 74.1,  longevity 88.7 โ’ 88.7,  sillage 92.8 โ’ 92.8)+- Iter 6: shifted 0.025 mL from Patchouli EO โ’ Ethylene Brassylate  (total 74.1 โ’ 74.1,  longevity 88.7 โ’ 88.7,  sillage 92.8 โ’ 92.8)+- Iter 7: shifted 0.025 mL from Geraniol โ’ Lime Distilled EO  (total 74.1 โ’ 74.1,  longevity 88.7 โ’ 88.8,  sillage 92.8 โ’ 92.5)+- Iter 8: shifted 0.025 mL from Norlimbanol Dextro โ’ Ethylene Brassylate  (total 74.1 โ’ 74.1,  longevity 88.8 โ’ 88.8,  sillage 92.5 โ’ 92.5)++## Build Rule++1. Blend the optimized concentrate first (base โ’ heart โ’ top).+2. Add `24.08 mL` ethanol 96 %.+3. Rest 4 weeks before serious judgement.diff --git a/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_III_Pamplemousse_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_III_Pamplemousse_Demachy_30mL_EdT.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..f35bb09--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_III_Pamplemousse_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md@@ -0,0 +1,241 @@+# Dior Homme Cologne III โ€” Pamplemousse โ€” Demachy Edition โ€” 30 mL EdT++**Batch:** 30.00 mL ยท ~16.7% EdT ยท **14 materials** (5 EOs/naturals)+**Profile:** DHC architecture ร— grapefruit as sole citrus โ€” the fruit-to-flower narrative+**Premise:** DHC I (bergamot) was the intellectual statement. DHC II (cedrat) was the artistic+extreme. DHC III is the one people fall in love with on first smell โ€” the warmest, most+immediately beautiful citrus in the line, made by letting a single plant tell its own story:+grapefruit rind at the opening, grapefruit blossom at the heart.+**Maceration:** 4 weeks minimum++---++## The Trilogy++| | DHC I | DHC II | DHC III |+|---|---|---|---|+| **Citrus** | Bergamot | Cedrat | **Grapefruit** |+| **Relationship to blossom** | Bergamot's linalool gently bridges to petitgrain | Cedrat's bitterness amplifies petitgrain's green โ€” productive tension | **Grapefruit rind fades โ’ grapefruit blossom rises. Same plant, two expressions. Seamless.** |+| **First-impression** | "Beautiful and refined" | "What IS that?" | **"That smells incredible"** |+| **Temperature** | Cool | Cold | **Bright โ€” the temperature of citrus itself** |+| **Wearer** | The connoisseur | The iconoclast | **The person who just wants to smell great** |++---++## Why Grapefruit, Why Now++Demachy rejected grapefruit for DHC II. Too meta, he said โ€” grapefruit citrus plus grapefruit+blossom makes a fragrance about grapefruit. He was right for DHC II. But for DHC III, the+brief is different: make something that smells good to most people on first sniff. The+single-plant narrative that was too conceptual for DHC II becomes the emotional core of DHC III.++Most people don't think about grapefruit blossom. They've never smelled it. What they know is+grapefruit โ€” the breakfast fruit, the pink half with sugar on top, the sharp-bitter-clean scent+that means morning, energy, freshness. When that familiar opening gives way to something softer+and greener โ€” but recognizably from the same plant โ€” the reaction isn't intellectual ("clever+concept") but visceral ("that's beautiful, what is it?").++The grapefruit rind-to-blossom transition is the fragrance's secret weapon. At first spray: that+zing of pink grapefruit, bright and cheerful โ€” everyone recognizes it, everyone likes it. Five+minutes later: the bitterness softens, a green-floral glow emerges. It's still grapefruit, but+transformed โ€” the way orange blossom relates to orange, but subtler because grapefruit blossom+is almost unknown in perfumery. The wearer's friends say "you smell amazing." The wearer's+partner says "you smell like you." Neither can identify the blossom as grapefruit โ€” they just+know it works.++---++## Equipment++- 1 amber glass bottle 30 mL+- 1 graduated pipette 1 mL (for 25โ€“1100 ยตL)+- 1 micro-pipette or 1 mL syringe graduated 0.01 mL (for 25โ€“50 ยตL)+- Ethanol 96% (perfumer's grade)++---++## Accord Architecture++### Layer 1 โ€” Grapefruit Rind (Top, ~29% of concentrate)+Grapefruit FCF at 22% of concentrate. Clean, bitter-pink, the smell of a grapefruit being peeled+in a bright kitchen. Linalyl Acetate at 7% bridges the citrus to the blossom โ€” grapefruit oil+contains linalyl acetate naturally, so this reinforcement reads as an extension of the rind's+own character, not a bergamot transplant. One citrus, unadorned. No aldehydes. No lemon. No+companion citrus. The grapefruit smells exactly like grapefruit โ€” and that's the point.++### Layer 2 โ€” Grapefruit Blossom, Full Bloom (Heart, ~43% of concentrate)+This is where DHC III earns its name. Petitgrain EO at 8% โ€” the green skeleton of the blossom.+Paradisamide at 0.4% active โ€” the tropical-grapefruit blossom character, the same molecule+that gave DHC I and II their signature. Ethyl Linalool at 9% โ€” the extended bridge that carries+the grapefruit's natural freshness into the blossom and beyond. Hedione at 20% + Hedione HC at+2.4% โ€” the radiance backbone that makes the blossom bloom outward rather than sit on skin.++The heart is the largest layer by design (43% of concentrate vs 28% base). This is a fragrance+about the blossom โ€” the rind is the introduction, but the blossom is the destination. For the+first time in the DHC line, the heart outranks the base in volume.++### Layer 3 โ€” Structured Musk, Restrained (Base, ~28% of concentrate)+The same OAV-balanced base from DHC II: Romandolide at 10% (projection, arm's length),+Ambrofix at 0.78% active (crystalline pillar, present but not dominant), Norlimbanol at 0.5%+(longevity scaffold), Vetival at 0.5% (suede-vetiver micro-texture). Four musks on three axes.+The base serves the blossom โ€” it provides longevity and projection without demanding attention.+After hour 3, when the grapefruit rind has faded and the blossom begins to thin, the structured+musk rises just enough to say "I'm still here" โ€” clean, warm, textured, but never loud.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer A: Base (heaviest first)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 500 | 500.0 | projection-axis musk โ€” arm's length, clean |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 400 | 400.0 | minimal skin cocoon โ€” 8% |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 250 | 250.0 | depth-axis musk โ€” lactonic creamy anchor |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 130 | 39.0 | crystalline-mineral pillar โ€” 0.78% active |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 | 5.0 | natural skin finish |+| 6 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 25 | 25.0 | Demachy longevity molecule โ€” transparent woody scaffold |+| 7 | Vetival | neat | 25 | 25.0 | Demachy texture โ€” suede-vetiver whisper |++**Base subtotal: ~1,380 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer B: Heart++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 1000 | 1000.0 | Demachy radiance โ€” 20%, the blossom blooms outward |+| 9 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 450 | 450.0 | extended bridge โ€” 9%, carries grapefruit freshness deep into the blossom |+| 10 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 400 | 400.0 | grapefruit blossom skeleton โ€” 8%, full volume |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 200 | 20.0 | grapefruit blossom character โ€” 0.4% active, DHC signature dose |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 120 | 120.0 | high-cis radiance โ€” 2.4%, superior jasmonate clarity |++**Heart subtotal: ~2,170 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer C: Top (most volatile, last)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 13 | Grapefruit FCF | neat | 1100 | 1100.0 | sole citrus โ€” the grapefruit rind, 22%. Immediately lovable opening |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 350 | 350.0 | bridge โ€” 7%, extends the rind's natural character into the blossom |++**Top subtotal: ~1,450 ยตL**++2. Concentrate is **~5,000 ยตL**; add approximately **25.0 mL ethanol 96%** (adjust visually to 30 mL line).+3. Cap tightly. Invert **50 times** โ€” gently, no shaking.+4. Label: **"Dior Homme Cologne III โ€” Pamplemousse โ€” Demachy โ€” macerate 4 weeks โ€” open after 2026-06-06"**++---++## Maceration++Store cool and dark. Invert gently once per week.+**Minimum 4 weeks.** Grapefruit FCF integrates faster than cedrat and slightly faster than bergamot+(less terpenic complexity). The expanded heart needs the full time โ€” hedione at 20% and ethyl+linalool at 9% take 2-3 weeks to cohere with the petitgrain-paradisamide blossom accord.+Norlimbanol + Vetival still need 3-4 weeks for full integration.++---++## Summary Table (14 materials)++### Base (7)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 500 |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 400 |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 250 |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 130 |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 |+| 6 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 25 |+| 7 | Vetival | neat | 25 |++### Heart (5)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 1000 |+| 9 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 450 |+| 10 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 400 |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 200 |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 120 |++### Top (2)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 13 | **Grapefruit FCF** | neat | **1100** |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 350 |++---++## Why Grapefruit at 22% (Not 28% Like Bergamot)++Grapefruit FCF has ODT 1.0 ppm โ€” 33% lower than bergamot's 1.5 ppm, meaning it's 50% more+perceptible per unit volume. At 1100 ยตL (22% of concentrate), grapefruit achieves OAV ~36,700+in final product โ€” already higher than bergamot's 31,111 at 1400 ยตL. Pushing grapefruit to+28% would push OAV past 46,000, making the opening aggressively bitter rather than cheerfully+bright. The 22% dose hits the sweet spot: unmistakably grapefruit, immediately appealing,+never punishing.++## The Key Materials, Recontextualized++### Petitgrain EO at 8% (up from 7% in DHC I/II)+With grapefruit rind as the opening, petitgrain isn't just providing a generic green-floral+bridge โ€” it's providing the GREEN STAGE of the grapefruit blossom accord. At 8%, it's the+loudest it's ever been in the DHC line, and it works because the context has shifted: petitgrain+is no longer a bridge between unrelated materials (bergamot โ’ grapefruit blossom), it IS the+blossom structure itself.++### Ethyl Linalool at 9% (way up from 6-7%)+With grapefruit's more volatile, less tenacious opening (grapefruit oil is higher in limonene,+lower in linalyl acetate than bergamot), the bridge needs to work harder. Ethyl Linalool at+9% extends the grapefruit's freshness into the heart and keeps the connection alive through+hour 4-5. This is the highest dose in any DHC formula, and it's the material that makes the+rind-to-blossom transition seamless rather than abrupt.++### Hedione at 20% (up from 19%)+The expanded heart needs more radiance. At 20%, hedione amplifies the grapefruit blossom+without adding a single identifiable floral note โ€” it just makes the blossom bloom outward,+reaching the nose of someone standing across the room who says "what smells so good?"++### Linalyl Acetate at 7% (up from 5%)+Grapefruit oil naturally contains less linalyl acetate than bergamot (~2-5% vs ~20-30%).+Adding LA at 7% brings the grapefruit opening closer to the structural bridge level that+petitgrain and ethyl linalool expect. Without this boost, the opening reads as "grapefruit+juice" (acidic, sharp) rather than "grapefruit perfume" (balanced, refined). This is the+single most important adjustment for making grapefruit work as a solitary citrus โ€” it+civilizes the rind.++---++## DHC III vs DHC I vs DHC II โ€” Side by Side++| | DHC I (Bergamot) | DHC II (Cedrat) | DHC III (Grapefruit) |+|---|---|---|---|+| **Top ยตL** | 1650 (33%) | 1650 (33%) | **1450 (29%)** |+| **Heart ยตL** | 1970 (39%) | 1970 (39%) | **2170 (43%)** |+| **Base ยตL** | 1380 (28%) | 1380 (28%) | **1380 (28%)** |+| **Star citrus** | Bergamot 1400 (28%) | Cedrat 1500 (30%) | **Grapefruit 1100 (22%)** |+| **Bridge dose** | LA 250 (5%) | LA 150 (3%) | **LA 350 (7%)** |+| **Bridge material** | Ethyl Linalool 350 | Ethyl Linalool 350 | **Ethyl Linalool 450 (9%)** |+| **Blossom** | Petitgrain 350, Paradisamide 0.4% | Petitgrain 350, Paradisamide 0.4% | **Petitgrain 400 (8%), Paradisamide 0.4%** |+| **Radiance** | Hedione 950 (19%) | Hedione 950 (19%) | **Hedione 1000 (20%)** |+| **Opening character** | Refined, classical, bergamot | Bitter, mineral, challenging | **Bright, cheerful, grapefruit โ€” the one that makes people smile** |+| **One-sentence pitch** | "What Dior Homme Cologne was always meant to be" | "For the person who finds bergamot too easy" | **"For everyone else โ€” the one that just smells amazing"** |++---++## OAV Layer Balance++| Layer | OAV sum (final product) | % of total |+|-------|------------------------|------------|+| TOP (grapefruit + LA) | 36,667 + 1,458 = 38,125 | 30.4% |+| HEART (hedione + petitgrain + ethyl linalool + paradisamide + HC) | 6,667 + 5,333 + 10,000 + 6,667 + 1,333 = 30,000 | 23.9% |+| BASE (musks + ambrofix + norlimbanol + vetival) | 16,667 + 6,667 + 4,167 + 26,000 + 333 + 8,333 + 1,667 = 57,167 | 45.6% |++The base is still the OAV leader (7 materials vs top's 2), but the heart+top combined+(54.3%) now exceeds the base (45.6%). For the first time in the DHC line, the citrus-blossom+complex carries more olfactory weight than the structured musk โ€” and that's what makes DHC III+smell so good on first sniff. The grapefruit opens, the blossom blooms, and the musk supports+rather than competes. This is the DHC architecture, fully realized.diff --git a/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_30mL_EdT.md b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_30mL_EdT.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..0c4bd23--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_30mL_EdT.md@@ -0,0 +1,289 @@+# Dior Homme Cologne II โ€” 30 mL Eau de Toilette Intense++**Batch:** 30.00 mL ยท ~16.7% EdT Intense ยท **16 materials** (4 EOs/naturals)+**Profile:** DHC I radical minimalism ร— Francis Kurkdjian aerial signature (hedione overdose, clean air, ambrox longevity)+**Creative direction:** If Franรงois Demachy's DHC (2013) is a single beam of light, Kurkdjian's DHC II+is that same light passing through a prism โ€” same bergamot-blossom-musk silhouette, now with an+invisible spectrum of aerial radiance, crystalline transparency, and extended tenacity.+**Positioning:** Standalone Dior Homme Cologne flanker. NOT Dior Homme Sport. NOT Dior Homme 2020.+**Maceration:** 3 weeks minimum++---++## Demachy vs Kurkdjian: Two Visions of DHC++| Axis | DHC I (Demachy, 2013) | DHC II (Kurkdjian, 2026) |+|------|----------------------|--------------------------|+| **Philosophy** | "Remove everything until only essence remains" | "Make the essence float โ€” give it air and time" |+| **Citrus** | Calabrian bergamot, solitary | Bergamot + lemon โ€” Kurkdjian's citrus duet (Petit Matin, Aqua Universalis) |+| **Heart** | Grapefruit blossom โ€” one floral, no radiance amplifier | Grapefruit blossom + hedione overdose (25% of concentrate) โ€” the blossom now extends 6 feet, not 6 inches |+| **Radiance** | None (DHC relies on bergamot's natural volatility) | Hedione + Hedione HC at 29% โ€” Kurkdjian's "aerial projection." The fragrance floats, it doesn't just sit |+| **Air** | None (DHC has no "air" materials) | Floralozone + Helional โ€” Kurkdjian's "clean air" accord (724 DNA). Not aquatic, not marine, not ozonic. Just the smell of air that's been cleaned by a thunderstorm |+| **Longevity** | 3โ€“4 hours (the Achilles heel) | 6โ€“8 hours โ€” Ambrox at 1.8% active creates a crystalline scaffold that holds the citrus-floral without weighing it down |+| **Musk** | Single white musk | 3-musk chord: Romandolide (projection) + EB (depth) + Ambrettolide (natural finish) |+| **Materials** | 3 visible, ~10 technical | 4 visible, 16 technical |+| **Signature** | "What a beautiful bergamot" | "What IS that?" โ€” the clean air accord is unidentifiable as a note |++---++## Why This Is NOT Dior Homme Sport (2021)++DHS 2021 (Kurkdjian's reboot): frankincense, elemi, pink pepper, cedar, vetiver. A woody-spicy-fresh.+DHC II: zero frankincense, zero pepper, zero cedar, zero vetiver. A citrus-radiant-musk.+Entirely different genre. The only shared element is Kurkdjian's hand โ€” the hedione overdose and the+aerial quality appear in both, but toward different destinations.++---++## Equipment++- 1 amber glass bottle 30 mL+- 1 graduated pipette 1 mL (for 30โ€“1250 ยตL)+- 1 micro-pipette or 1 mL syringe graduated 0.01 mL (for 30โ€“40 ยตL)+- Ethanol 96% (perfumer's grade)++---++## Accord Architecture++### Layer 1 โ€” Citrus Duet (Top, ~28.6% of concentrate)+DHC I uses solitary bergamot. Kurkdjian adds lemon โ€” his signature move (Petit Matin, Aqua+Universalis Forte). The lemon doesn't compete with bergamot; it creates a "citrus chord" that+reads as more three-dimensional. Bergamot at 18% is still the lead. Lemon at 5% is the brightener.+Linalyl Acetate extends both into the heart. Aldehyde C10 at 0.0006% active provides invisible+sparkle โ€” a Kurkdjian micro-touch, not a Chanel aldehydic statement.++### Layer 2 โ€” Grapefruit Blossom + Aerial Radiance (Heart, ~44.8% of concentrate)+This is where DHC II earns its name. The grapefruit blossom (Petitgrain + Paradisamide) is the+same DHC heart, but Kurkdjian wraps it in a massive hedione veil. Hedione at 25% + Hedione HC at+4% = 29% hedione total โ€” this is Kurkdjian's aerial signature. The blossom doesn't just sit on skin;+it diffuses into the air around the wearer. Ethyl Linalool extends the bergamot freshness into the+base with woody-floral tenacity. Floralozone at 0.2% active + Helional at 1.2% create Kurkdjian's+"clean air" accord โ€” the olfactory equivalent of opening a window after rain. Not aquatic, not marine,+not ozonic โ€” just the smell of air that has no smell, made perceptible.++### Layer 3 โ€” Crystalline Musk + Ambrox Scaffold (Base, ~26.6% of concentrate)+DHC I's weakness is longevity. Kurkdjian's fix: Ambrox. Not Sauvage's nose-punch Ambrox (that's+Demachy's 10% Ambrox Super), but Kurkdjian's Ambrox โ€” crystalline, transparent, a scaffold rather+than a note. At 1.8% active, it creates an invisible skeleton that holds the citrus-floral for+6-8 hours without adding weight or woodiness. This is the same trick Kurkdjian used in 724 and+Aqua Universalis. The white musks are clean and projecting: Romandolide for diffusive sillage,+Ethylene Brassylate for lactonic depth, Ambrettolide at micro-dose for natural skin finish.+Iso E Super at 6% is the minimal skin cocoon โ€” Kurkdjian uses less IES than Demachy; he prefers+Ambrox for the skin-effect register.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer A: Base (heaviest first)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 540 | 540.0 | projection white musk โ€” clean diffusive sillage |+| 2 | Ambrofix | 30% | 300 | 90.0 | Kurkdjian crystalline scaffold โ€” longevity without weight |+| 3 | Iso E Super | neat | 300 | 300.0 | minimal skin cocoon โ€” Kurkdjian prefers Ambrox for this register |+| 4 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 150 | 150.0 | depth-axis musk โ€” lactonic clean anchor |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 40 | 4.0 | natural skin finish โ€” Kurkdjian's elegance touch |++**Base subtotal: ~1,330 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer B: Heart++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 6 | Hedione | neat | 1250 | 1250.0 | Kurkdjian aerial signature โ€” 25% of concentrate. The blossom floats |+| 7 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 250 | 250.0 | grapefruit blossom skeleton โ€” DHC I DNA |+| 8 | Hedione HC | neat | 200 | 200.0 | high-cis radiance โ€” superior jasmonate bloom (8ร— standard) |+| 9 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 200 | 200.0 | woody-floral bridge โ€” extends bergamot freshness into base |+| 10 | Paradisamide | 10% | 180 | 18.0 | grapefruit blossom character โ€” DHC I DNA, the signature molecule |+| 11 | Floralozone | 10% | 100 | 10.0 | Kurkdjian "clean air" accord โ€” 724 DNA, the air after rain |+| 12 | Helional | neat | 60 | 60.0 | watery-transparent freshness โ€” complements the clean air accord |++**Heart subtotal: ~2,240 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer C: Top (most volatile, last)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 13 | Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 900 | 900.0 | DHC I bergamot โ€” still the lead citrus |+| 14 | Lemon FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 250 | 250.0 | Kurkdjian citrus duet โ€” Petit Matin/Aqua Universalis energy |+| 15 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 250 | 250.0 | bergamot companion โ€” extends both citruses into the heart |+| 16 | Aldehyde C10 | 1% | 30 | 0.30 | micro-sparkle โ€” Kurkdjian uses aldehydes at the threshold of silence |++**Top subtotal: ~1,430 ยตL**++2. Concentrate is **~5,000 ยตL**; add approximately **25.0 mL ethanol 96%** (adjust visually to 30 mL line).+3. Cap tightly. Invert **50 times** โ€” gently, no shaking.+4. Label: **"Dior Homme Cologne II โ€” 2026-05-09 โ€” macerate 3 weeks โ€” open after 2026-05-30"**++---++## Maceration++Store cool and dark. Invert gently once per week.+**Minimum 3 weeks.** The hedione-Floralozone-Helional air accord needs time to integrate with the+citrus opening. Ambrox + musk base reaches full coherence at 2โ€“3 weeks. The bergamot-lemon duet+softens at week 1. The "clean air" effect blooms at week 2 and reaches full transparency at week 3.++---++## Summary Table (all 16 materials)++### Base (5)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 540 |+| 2 | Ambrofix | 30% | 300 |+| 3 | Iso E Super | neat | 300 |+| 4 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 150 |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 40 |++### Heart (7)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 6 | Hedione | neat | 1250 |+| 7 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 250 |+| 8 | Hedione HC | neat | 200 |+| 9 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 200 |+| 10 | Paradisamide | 10% | 180 |+| 11 | Floralozone | 10% | 100 |+| 12 | Helional | neat | 60 |++### Top (4)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 13 | Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 900 |+| 14 | Lemon FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 250 |+| 15 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 250 |+| 16 | Aldehyde C10 | 1% | 30 |++---++## Material Selection โ€” Dior II Justifications++### Why Lemon added (Kurkdjian citrus duet)+Demachy's DHC uses solitary bergamot. Kurkdjian's fragrance philosophy rejects the solitary citrus โ€”+he builds citrus chords (Petit Matin: litsea cubeba + lemon + orange blossom; Aqua Universalis:+bergamot + lemon + white flowers; 724: bergamot + aldehydes). Lemon at 5% adds brightness without+competing with bergamot's refinement. It makes the opening less "single-note citrus" and more+"citrus accord" โ€” three-dimensional where DHC I is one-dimensional.++### Why not Cedrat instead of Lemon+Cedrat is bitter-mineral. Kurkdjian's citruses are bright-juicy, not bitter-mineral (that's an Ellena/+Hermes register). Lemon is Kurkdjian's choice โ€” see Petit Matin's lemon opening. Cedrat would make+this read as "Ellena does Dior" rather than "Kurkdjian does Dior."++### Why Hedione at 25% (Kurkdjian aerial signature)+This is the single most important Kurkdjian decision in the formula. Demachy used zero hedione in+DHC โ€” the fragrance has no radiance amplifier; it relies purely on bergamot's natural volatility.+Kurkdjian uses hedione at 15-30% in virtually every composition. At 25%, hedione creates "aerial+projection" โ€” the fragrance doesn't just evaporate from skin; it diffuses into a transparent cloud+around the wearer. This is what makes DHC II last longer (the hedione cloud holds the blossom aloft+for hours after the bergamot has evaporated) and project better (the cloud extends the scent bubble).++### Why Hedione HC in addition+Standard Hedione provides volume; HC provides brilliance. At 200 ยตL (4%), HC doubles the radiance+efficiency โ€” the equivalent of 1600 ยตL of standard Hedione. Kurkdjian would appreciate the economy+and the cleaner high-cis jasmonate bloom.++### Why Floralozone + Helional (the clean air accord)+Kurkdjian's 724 is built around a "clean air" accord โ€” aldehydes + white florals + a transparent+ozonic-marine material. Floralozone is the closest inventory equivalent: it's a fresh-clean-ozonic+floralizer that creates a "just-cleaned air" effect without reading as aquatic or marine. Helional+adds a watery-transparent layer that prevents Floralozone from reading as "laundry." Together at+0.2% + 1.2%, they create Kurkdjian's signature "air that has been cleaned by a thunderstorm" โ€”+perceptible but unidentifiable. Rejected: Calone (depleted; also too marine, reads as "sport" not+"clean air"), Scentenal (too metallic-ozone, reads as industrial rather than natural), Triplal (too+aggressive). ++### Why Ambrofix at 1.8% active (Kurkdjian crystalline scaffold)+This is Kurkdjian's longevity trick. Demachy's DHC has no fixative beyond its white musk โ€” it lasts+3-4 hours. Ambrox at 1.8% active creates a crystalline skeleton that holds the citrus-floral for+6-8 hours. This is NOT Sauvage ambrox โ€” Sauvage (Demachy) uses Ambrox at much higher doses where+it reads as a distinct "amber" note. At 1.8% active, Kurkdjian's Ambrox is a scaffold, not a note โ€”+you don't smell it; you feel it holding the fragrance together. Rejected: Ambrox Super (depleted),+Ambermax (too warm-rounded, reads as amber rather than structure), Amberwood F (too transparent to+scaffold at any dose), Azarbre (too warm, adds cedar-amber character Kurkdjian doesn't use in fresh+compositions).++### Why Ambrettolide (Kurkdjian elegance)+Kurkdjian's fragrances always have an elegant skin-finish. 724 uses a specific clean-skin musk.+Ambrettolide at 0.08% active provides the most naturalistic skin warmth in inventory โ€” it makes the+drydown smell like "this person is naturally clean" rather than "this person is wearing cologne."+Rejected: Habanolide (too warm-intimate; reads as "blanket" rather than "clean skin"), Exaltolide+(depleted; also too fatty-skin), Galaxolide (polycyclic laundry โ€” contradicts the naturalistic+direction), Zenolide (too cold-citrus; works against the clean-air accord rather than with it).++### Why no Habanolide+DHC I uses a cold white musk. DHC II follows the same register: Romandolide (clean projection) is+the correct primary musk. Habanolide's warm-skin intimacy would add a "blanket" register that+contradicts the aerial, crystalline concept. Kurkdjian's 724 and Aqua Universalis use clean, cold,+crystalline musks โ€” not warm-intimate ones.++### What was deliberately excluded+- **Damascenone / rose materials**: DHC has zero rose. Kurkdjian wouldn't add it โ€” rose belongs to+  Chanel's classical floral DNA, not Dior's modern minimalism. Kurkdjian's fresh fragrances (724,+  Aqua Universalis, Petit Matin) don't use rose-ketones.+- **Alpha Irone / iris materials**: DHC has zero iris. The original Dior Homme (2005) is the iris+  fragrance. Adding iris to DHC II would cannibalize the original Dior Homme's territory.+- **Oranger Crystals / orange blossom**: Petit Matin uses orange blossom heavily, but DHC's heart+  is grapefruit blossom, not orange blossom. Neroli would shift the genre toward white floral.+- **Jasmine FO, Ylang EO**: Classical French floral materials. Dior's modern direction (Demachy,+  Kurkdjian) avoids traditional florals in the Homme line. These belong to Chanel, not Dior.+- **Vetiver, Evernyl**: Chanel woody-chypre signature. Dior Homme Cologne has zero woody-chypre+  character. Dior Homme 2020 has woods; DHC II does not.+- **Coumarin, Vanillin, Ethyl Maltol**: DHC is not sweet. Kurkdjian keeps it this way.+- **Black Pepper, Cardamom, Juniper**: Spicy-aromatic lift belongs to Dior Homme Sport (2021) and+  Sauvage. DHC II is not spicy.+- **Lavender, Geranium, Clary Sage**: Fougere materials. Belongs to Dior Homme 2020 and Sauvage.+  Not DHC territory.+- **Cashmeran, Azarbre, Timberol, Norlimbanol, Kephalis, Clearwood, Vertofix, Koavone**: All+  structural woods and woody-ambers. DHC I has zero wood. DHC II keeps zero wood. Ambrox provides+  structure without woodiness.+- **Dihydromyrcenol**: Laundry-clean freshness. This is Dior Homme Sport territory (Demachy's+  version used DHM heavily). Kurkdjian's fresh fragrances use hedione + air accord instead.+- **Calone**: Marine-sport direction. Contradicts the "clean air" accord which is intended to be+  neither marine nor sport.++---++## Key OAV Estimates (concentrate)++| Material | Conc in conc (ppm) | Approx ODT | OAV | Perception |+|----------|--------------------|------------|-----|------------|+| Bergamot FCF Sicilian | 180,000 | ~14 ppm | ~12,900 | Massive dominant opening |+| Hedione (total) | 290,000 | ~50 ppm | ~5,800 | Kurkdjian aerial radiance โ€” extreme |+| Romandolide | 108,000 | ~2 ppm | ~54,000 | Very dominant projection musk |+| Lemon FCF Sicilian | 50,000 | ~5 ppm | ~10,000 | Bright citrus energy โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Petitgrain EO | 50,000 | ~5 ppm | ~10,000 | Grapefruit blossom โ€” DHC DNA |+| Paradisamide (active) | 3,600 | ~0.05 ppb | ~72,000,000 | Blossom signature โ€” extreme impact |+| Ambrofix (active) | 18,000 | ~0.3 ppb | ~60,000,000 | Crystalline scaffold โ€” extreme impact at ppb ODT |+| Iso E Super | 60,000 | ~0.5 ppm | ~120,000 | Strong skin cocoon |+| Floralozone (active) | 2,000 | ~0.005 ppm | ~400,000 | Clean air โ€” powerfully perceptible despite low concentration |+| Helional | 12,000 | ~0.1 ppm | ~120,000 | Watery transparency โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Ethyl Linalool | 40,000 | ~0.5 ppm | ~80,000 | Strong woody-floral bridge |+| Ambrettolide (active) | 800 | ~0.01 ppm | ~80,000 | Natural skin warmth โ€” perceptible elegance |+| Linalyl Acetate | 50,000 | ~1 ppm | ~50,000 | Citrus-extending freshness |+| Ethylene Brassylate | 30,000 | ~1 ppm | ~30,000 | Strong lactonic depth |+| Aldehyde C10 (active) | 60 | ~0.5 ppb | ~120,000 | Micro-sparkle โ€” perceptible at opening |+| Hedione HC | 40,000 | ~15 ppm | ~2,667 | Superior radiance โ€” clean jasmonate bloom |++*OAVs are in concentrate. After ~6ร— dilution in ethanol, divide all values by 6.*++---++## Comparison: All Four Formulas++| | Seuil du Jour v3 | Transparence (Chanel) | **DHC II (Dior)** |+|---|---|---|---|+| **Materials** | 18 | 22 | **16** |+| **Citrus** | 1 (bergamot) | 2 (bergamot + cedrat) | **2 (bergamot + lemon)** |+| **Heart innovation** | Rose halo + orris whisper | Chanel floral trinity + iris | **Kurkdjian aerial radiance + clean air** |+| **Base** | Clean musk + micro-ebanol | Musk chord + vetiver + evernyl | **Ambrox scaffold + clean musk** |+| **Projection** | Moderate | Moderate-intimate | **Aerial (hedione cloud)** |+| **Longevity** | 4โ€“5 hr | 5โ€“6 hr | **6โ€“8 hr (ambrox scaffold)** |+| **Class signifiers** | Damascenone + Alpha Irone | Aldehydes + jasmine-rose-ylang + iris | **Floralozone air + hedione aeriality** |+| **Philosophy** | Independent niche โ€” owns its luxury | Chanel heritage โ€” transparent version of No. 5 DNA | **Kurkdjian modernism โ€” DHC evolved, not referenced** |diff --git a/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_Cedrat_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_Cedrat_Demachy_30mL_EdT.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..430bfe3--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_Cedrat_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md@@ -0,0 +1,207 @@+# Dior Homme Cologne II โ€” Cรฉdrat โ€” Demachy Edition โ€” 30 mL EdT++**Batch:** 30.00 mL ยท ~16.7% EdT ยท **14 materials** (5 EOs/naturals)+**Premise:** Dior tells Demachy: same DHC II structure, but no bergamot. Use a different citrus.+**Demachy's choice:** Cedrat FCF Sicilian โ€” bitter citron. The coldest, most mineral citrus in+existence. Where bergamot is DHC's linen suit, cedrat is its steel-and-glass tower.+**Maceration:** 4 weeks minimum++---++## Why Cedrat++Demachy was given a choice and chose the hardest one.++**Rejected alternatives:**+- **Lemon** โ€” too classical, too obvious. Every house has a lemon cologne. Demachy doesn't do obvious.+- **Grapefruit** โ€” too meta. The grapefruit blossom is already the heart. Grapefruit citrus + grapefruit blossom = a fragrance about grapefruit. Demachy doesn't do conceptual.+- **Blood Orange** โ€” too warm, too juicy. DHC is cold-transparent, not warm-fruity. Blood orange pulls toward gourmand.+- **Red Mandarin** โ€” too sweet-tangerine. Pulls toward oriental. Wrong genre entirely.+- **Lime** โ€” too cocktail, too sharp-acidic. Reads as a summer drink, not a perfume.+- **D-Limonene** โ€” a molecule, not a material. Demachy works with naturals, not single-molecule approximations.++**Why cedrat:**+Cedrat is the citrus for people who find bergamot too easy. It's bitter where bergamot is bright,+mineral where bergamot is floral, cold where bergamot is warm. It's the citrus that asks the+wearer to meet it halfway โ€” and Demachy has always made fragrances that respect the wearer's+intelligence.++The cedrat + grapefruit blossom pairing creates a DOUBLE BITTER accord โ€” the most severe,+transparent citrus opening in the Dior Homme line. Where the original DHC is "I just showered,"+the cedrat DHC is "I just showered in a glass building in Zurich." Same cleanliness, different+architecture.++---++## Bergamot DHC vs Cedrat DHC++| Axis | Bergamot DHC II | Cedrat DHC II |+|------|----------------|---------------|+| **Citrus character** | Refined, bright, floral-linalool. Universally loved. | Bitter, mineral, cold-citron. Challenging. |+| **Opening effect** | "Expensive bergamot" โ€” recognizable, welcoming | "What IS that citrus?" โ€” unfamiliar, intriguing |+| **Citrus-blossom relationship** | Bergamot's linalool smoothly bridges to petitgrain's green-floral | Cedrat's bitterness amplifies petitgrain's green-bitterness. Double bitter. No smooth transition โ€” a stark handoff |+| **Temperature** | Cool | **Cold** โ€” 2-3ยฐC colder on the skin |+| **Hedione adjustment** | 16% (700 ยตL) | **17% (850 ยตL)** โ€” slightly more radiance to compensate for cedrat's severity |+| **Paradisamide adjustment** | 0.4% active (200 ยตL of 10%) | **0.3% active (150 ยตL of 10%)** โ€” reduced to prevent the double-bitter grapefruit-on-grapefruit amplification |+| **Wearer** | Wants to smell refined and approachable | Wants to smell refined and untouchable |+| **Season** | Spring/summer, day | Summer, day-to-evening. Works in hot weather where bergamot reads as too soft |++---++## Equipment++- 1 amber glass bottle 30 mL+- 1 graduated pipette 1 mL (for 25โ€“1500 ยตL)+- 1 micro-pipette or 1 mL syringe graduated 0.01 mL (for 25โ€“50 ยตL)+- Ethanol 96% (perfumer's grade)++---++## Accord Architecture++### Layer 1 โ€” Solitary Cedrat (Top, ~33% of concentrate)+Cedrat FCF Sicilian at 30% of concentrate. Solitary, massive, unapologetic โ€” the same structural+approach as the bergamot original, but a completely different olfactory character. Cedrat is+bitter citron โ€” the fruit that looks like a lumpy lemon but smells colder, more mineral, less+acidic. Linalyl Acetate at 3% (150 ยตL) โ€” sufficient to bridge the citrus to the blossom without+adding bergamot character. The cedrat-petitgrain handoff is clean: bitter citrus fades, green+bitterness rises to meet it.++### Layer 2 โ€” Grapefruit Blossom, Full Volume (Heart, ~39% of concentrate)+The OAV-balanced heart. Petitgrain EO at 7% โ€” the full grapefruit blossom skeleton, no longer+pulled back for fear of double-bitter aggression. Paradisamide at 0.4% active โ€” the full DHC+signature dose, the blossom is back to full character. Hedione at 19% + Hedione HC at 2.4% โ€”+the radiance backbone carries the blossom through the lighter base. Ethyl Linalool at 7% โ€”+a longer bridge between the expanded heart and the reduced base, keeping the citrus-floral+connection alive through hour 4-5.++### Layer 3 โ€” Structured Musk, OAV-Balanced (Base, ~28% of concentrate)+The base has been lightened to correct the OAV imbalance. Romandolide at 10% (down from 14%) โ€”+projection at arm's length, not room-filling. Ambrofix at 0.78% active (down from 1.2%) โ€”+crystalline pillar present but no longer dominant. The base total OAV has been reduced from+64% of the formula to approximately 42% โ€” still substantial (musks are always base-heavy),+but no longer overwhelming the citrus-blossom layers. Norlimbanol at 0.5% for longevity,+Vetival at 0.5% for micro-texture. Four musks on three axes (Romandolide projection, EB+lactonic depth, Ambrettolide natural finish). The base now supports without dominating.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer A: Base (heaviest first)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 500 | 500.0 | projection-axis musk โ€” diffusive, clean. Reduced from 14% to 10% for OAV balance |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 400 | 400.0 | minimal skin cocoon โ€” 8%, restrained |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 250 | 250.0 | depth-axis musk โ€” lactonic creamy anchor |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 130 | 39.0 | crystalline-mineral pillar โ€” 0.78% active, down from 1.2% to prevent base dominance |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 | 5.0 | natural skin finish |+| 6 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 25 | 25.0 | Demachy longevity molecule โ€” transparent woody scaffold |+| 7 | Vetival | neat | 25 | 25.0 | Demachy texture โ€” suede-vetiver whisper |++**Base subtotal: ~1,380 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer B: Heart++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 950 | 950.0 | Demachy radiance โ€” 19%, strengthened to carry more of the formula's volume as the base lightens |+| 9 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 350 | 350.0 | grapefruit blossom skeleton โ€” 7%, restored to full volume |+| 10 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 350 | 350.0 | bergamot-blossom-to-base bridge โ€” 7%, strengthened for a longer bridge span |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 200 | 20.0 | grapefruit blossom character โ€” 0.4% active, restored to full DHC signature dose |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 120 | 120.0 | high-cis radiance โ€” superior jasmonate clarity, 2.4% |++**Heart subtotal: ~1,970 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer C: Top (most volatile, last)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 13 | Cedrat FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 1500 | 1500.0 | Demachy's alternative citrus โ€” bitter citron. Solitary, massive, unapologetic. 30% of concentrate |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 150 | 150.0 | bridge โ€” increased from 100 to 150 ยตL (3%) for stronger citrus-to-blossom transition |++**Top subtotal: ~1,650 ยตL**++2. Concentrate is **~5,000 ยตL**; add approximately **25.0 mL ethanol 96%** (adjust visually to 30 mL line).+3. Cap tightly. Invert **50 times** โ€” gently, no shaking.+4. Label: **"Dior Homme Cologne II โ€” Cรฉdrat โ€” Demachy โ€” macerate 4 weeks โ€” open after 2026-06-06"**++---++## Maceration++Store cool and dark. Invert gently once per week.+**Minimum 4 weeks.** The same as the bergamot version. Cedrat integrates faster than bergamot+(less terpenic complexity to settle) โ€” but Norlimbanol + Vetival still need the full 3-4 weeks.+The hedione-clarity adjustment benefits from the extra time.++---++## Summary Table (14 materials)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 500 |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 400 |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 250 |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 130 |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 |+| 6 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 25 |+| 7 | Vetival | neat | 25 |+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 950 |+| 9 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 350 |+| 10 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 350 |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 200 |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 120 |+| 13 | **Cedrat FCF oil Sicilian** | neat | **1500** |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 150 |++---++## Key Adjustments vs Bergamot DHC II++| # | Material | Bergamot version | Cedrat v1 (unbalanced) | Cedrat v2 (balanced) | Reason |+|---|----------|-----------------|----------------------|---------------------|--------|+| 13 | Citrus | Bergamot 1400 ยตL | Cedrat 1500 ยตL | Cedrat 1500 ยตL | Cedrat is less dense per unit of olfactory impact. 30% is needed to match bergamot's 28% perceived strength |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | 250 ยตL | 100 ยตL | **150 ยตL** | v1 was too stark โ€” the citrus-to-blossom transition lacked bridge. 150 ยตL restores a cleaner handoff without making cedrat smell like bergamot |+| 1 | Romandolide | 700 ยตL | 700 ยตL | **500 ยตL** | v1 base OAV was 64% of total. Romandolide at 14% drove excessive projection. 10% is correct for EdT cologne โ€” projects arm's length, not room-filling |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 200 ยตL | 200 ยตL | **130 ยตL** | v1 Ambrofix OAV 40,000 dominated the base. 0.78% active still provides crystalline longevity without overwhelming the citrus opening |+| 2 | Iso E Super | 450 ยตL | 450 ยตL | **400 ยตL** | Minor reduction โ€” 8% IES is sufficient for skin adhesion without adding to base weight |+| 8 | Hedione | 700 ยตL (14%) | 850 ยตL (17%) | **950 ยตL (19%)** | Base lightening freed volume for the heart. Hedione carries more of the formula's radiance, keeping the blossom afloat longer |+| 9 | Petitgrain | 350 ยตL | 300 ยตL | **350 ยตL** | v1 reduced petitgrain fearing double-bitter aggression. With a lighter base, the full 7% petitgrain is balanced โ€” the bitterness now has space to breathe |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 200 ยตL (10%) | 150 ยตL (10%) | **200 ยตL (10%)** | Restored to full DHC signature dose. The base no longer competes; the blossom can be itself |+| 10 | Ethyl Linalool | 300 ยตL | 300 ยตL | **350 ยตL** | Strengthened bridge between expanded heart and lighter base |+| 12 | Hedione HC | 100 ยตL | 100 ยตL | **120 ยตL** | Slight boost for superior jasmonate clarity in the expanded heart |++---++## The Cedrat Character: What Changes, What Doesn't++**What changes:**+- Opening: from "beautiful bergamot" to "what IS that citrus?" Cedrat is unfamiliar to most people. The opening is a question, not an answer.+- Temperature: 2-3ยฐC colder on skin. Cedrat reads as mineral-cold; bergamot reads as cool-bright.+- Bitterness: significantly more bitter. The cedrat-petitgrain double bitterness creates a very dry, very transparent effect โ€” like the difference between still water (bergamot) and sparkling water (cedrat).+- Approachability: reduced. This is a fragrance for people who find the original DHC too ingratiating.+- Recognition: lower. No one will say "cedrat!" โ€” they'll say "what is that?" and then "I want it."++**What doesn't change:**+- Structure: 14 materials, same base, same heart skeleton, same longevity (6-7 hours).+- Cleanliness: still an "I just showered" fragrance. Different soap, same cleanliness.+- Drydown: after hour 3, the cedrat and bergamot versions converge. The citrus is gone; what remains is the structured musk base (Norlimbanol + Vetival + musks). A person testing both on different arms would find them identical after hour 4.+- Price point / positioning: same Dior Homme Cologne line, different flanker.++---++## Why This Is Demachy's Choice, Not Marketing's++Marketing would choose lemon. It's safe, recognizable, universally liked. Demachy chooses cedrat+because it says something new while staying within his aesthetic. The cedrat DHC is colder, more+severe, more transparent โ€” it pushes the DHC concept further than bergamot allowed. Where bergamot+is DHC's commercial face, cedrat is DHC's artistic statement.++This is the difference between a perfumer and a brand manager: the brand manager says "what citrus+tests well?" The perfumer says "what citrus creates the most interesting version of this idea?"+For Demachy, the interesting version is the one that makes people ask questions.diff --git a/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_Demachy_30mL_EdT.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..b8c6623--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_II_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md@@ -0,0 +1,305 @@+# Dior Homme Cologne II โ€” Demachy Edition โ€” 30 mL EdT++**Batch:** 30.00 mL ยท ~16.7% EdT ยท **14 materials** (5 EOs/naturals)+**Profile:** DHC I radical minimalism, extended โ€” Demachy evolves his own creation+**Creative direction:** Demachy doesn't add notes. He adds structure. DHC I's problem was never its+opening or heart โ€” those are perfect. The problem was the base: anonymous white musk, 3-hour lifespan,+nothing to discover after the bergamot fades. DHC II keeps the same bergamot and grapefruit blossom,+but replaces the generic white musk with a structured, textured base that lasts 6-7 hours and rewards+the wearer who notices what happens after hour 3.+**Maceration:** 4 weeks minimum++---++## Demachy Fixing His Own Work++DHC I (2013) was Demachy's most radical statement: a 3-note fragrance that proved luxury could be+found in absence. But he knew the weaknesses:++1. **3-4 hour longevity** โ€” bergamot flashes off, grapefruit blossom holds for 90 minutes, then nothing but white musk+2. **Boring drydown** โ€” after the blossom fades, it's just clean. No texture. No discovery.+3. **No projection** โ€” DHC I is a skin scent from minute one. Beautiful for the wearer, invisible to everyone else.++DHC II addresses all three without adding a single new "note." No lemon (Kurkdjian). No iris (original+Dior Homme). No rose (Chanel). No aldehydes. No clean-air accord. No decoration.++**The Demachy solution:** Replace the anonymous white musk with four structural base materials that+do what the white musk couldn't โ€” project, persist, and reward attention.++| Problem | Demachy's Fix | Material |+|---------|--------------|----------|+| No longevity | Transparent woody-amber scaffold at micro-dose | **Norlimbanol Dextro** at 0.5% โ€” Demachy's longevity molecule (used in Fahrenheit Parfum, Dior Homme 2020). Powerfully perceptible at ppb levels. Adds 3-4 hours without adding wood character |+| No projection | Replace DHC I's intimate white musk with a diffusive macrocyclic | **Romandolide** at 10% โ€” clean projection musk. Extends the scent bubble from skin-only to arm's-length |+| Boring drydown | Add micro-texture that rewards the curious | **Vetival** at 0.5% โ€” suede-vetiver dryness. Demachy's love of vetiver (Vetiver Dior, Eau Sauvage Parfum) expressed as a whisper โ€” not a note, a texture. The person leaning in notices something they can't name |+| Grapefruit blossom fades too fast | Extend the blossom into the base | **Ethyl Linalool** bridges bergamot's linalool to the woody base. **Paradisamide** at 0.4% active โ€” the same blossom molecule, persistent enough to survive into hour 4-5 |++---++## Demachy vs Kurkdjian vs Chanel++| Axis | Demachy DHC II | Kurkdjian DHC II | Chanel Transparence |+|------|---------------|-----------------|---------------------|+| **Citrus** | ONE bergamot. Massive, solitary. | Bergamot + lemon duet | Bergamot + cedrat + aldehydes |+| **Heart** | Grapefruit blossom. Hedione at 16% โ€” structural, not aerial. | Grapefruit blossom. Hedione at 29% โ€” aerial cloud. Floralozone air accord | Grapefruit blossom + jasmine-rose-ylang whisper + iris |+| **Base** | 4-musk chord + Norlimbanol (woody longevity) + Vetival (texture) | 3-musk chord + Ambrox scaffold (crystalline longevity) | 4-musk chord + Vetiver + Evernyl (chypre) |+| **Longevity trick** | Norlimbanol โ€” transparent woody, barely perceptible as a note, extreme tenacity | Ambrox overdose โ€” crystalline scaffold, perceptible as "clean mineral" | Vetiver + Evernyl โ€” classical chypre structure |+| **Projection** | Moderate โ€” arm's length. Romandolide diffusive musk at 10% | High โ€” hedione cloud creates 6-foot scent bubble | Moderate-intimate โ€” Chanel is quieter |+| **Materials** | 14 | 16 | 22 |+| **Philosophy** | "Add structure, not notes" | "Add air and time" | "Add heritage and seamlessness" |++---++## Equipment++- 1 amber glass bottle 30 mL+- 1 graduated pipette 1 mL (for 25โ€“1400 ยตL)+- 1 micro-pipette or 1 mL syringe graduated 0.01 mL (for 25โ€“50 ยตL)+- Ethanol 96% (perfumer's grade)++---++## Accord Architecture++### Layer 1 โ€” Solitary Bergamot (Top, ~33% of concentrate)+DHC I uses Calabrian bergamot alone. DHC II keeps this โ€” the signature is non-negotiable.+Bergamot FCF Sicilian at 28% of concentrate. Linalyl Acetate at 5% extends the bergamot's+natural linalyl acetate content (bergamot EO is ~20-30% linalyl acetate naturally). No aldehydes.+No lemon. No cedrat. One citrus, unadorned.++### Layer 2 โ€” Grapefruit Blossom Extended (Heart, ~39% of concentrate)+Petitgrain EO at 7% is the grapefruit blossom skeleton. Paradisamide at 0.4% active is the blossom+character โ€” the same molecule Demachy used in DHC I, now slightly elevated for better persistence+into the base. Hedione at 19% is structural radiance โ€” strengthened to carry more volume as the+base lightens. Hedione HC at 2.4% for superior jasmonate clarity. Ethyl Linalool at 7% bridges+bergamot's linalool into the woody base โ€” the extended bridge that keeps the citrus-floral+connection alive through hour 4-5.++### Layer 3 โ€” Structured, Textured Musk, OAV-Balanced (Base, ~28% of concentrate)+Four musks on three axes: Romandolide at 10% (projection, arm's length โ€” down from 14%),+Ethylene Brassylate at 5% (lactonic depth), Ambrettolide at 0.1% active (natural skin finish).+Iso E Super at 8% for the minimal skin cocoon. Ambrofix at 0.78% active provides crystalline+transparency โ€” reduced from 1.2% to prevent the base from overwhelming the citrus opening.+The base was OAV-balanced: the original had base OAV at 60% of total; after correction, base+is ~52%, heart ~22%, top ~26%.++The two Demachy-specific additions (unchanged):+- **Norlimbanol Dextro at 0.5%** โ€” transparent woody longevity. Not a wood note. Not perceptible+  as "cedar" or "sandalwood." Perceptible only as the fragrance's refusal to disappear after hour 4.+  Demachy used similar super-amber materials (AmberXtreme, Ambrocenide) in Fahrenheit Parfum and+  Dior Homme 2020. At this dose, it's a scaffold, not a note.+- **Vetival at 0.5%** โ€” suede-vetiver micro-texture. Demachy's lifelong love of vetiver (Vetiver+  Dior, Eau Sauvage Parfum, Granville) expressed as a whisper. At this dose, it's not "vetiver" โ€”+  it's the barest suggestion of dry-suede texture that rewards the person who leans in after hour 3.+  Without it, the drydown is just "clean." With it, the drydown is "clean, and also something+  interesting I can't identify."++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer A: Base (heaviest first)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 500 | 500.0 | projection-axis musk โ€” diffusive, arm's length. Reduced from 14% to 10% for OAV balance |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 400 | 400.0 | minimal skin cocoon โ€” Demachy uses IES at low-moderate doses, 8% |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 250 | 250.0 | depth-axis musk โ€” lactonic creamy anchor |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 130 | 39.0 | crystalline-mineral pillar โ€” 0.78% active, reduced to prevent base OAV dominance |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 | 5.0 | natural skin finish โ€” Demachy's elegance; the most naturalistic musk |+| 6 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 25 | 25.0 | Demachy longevity molecule โ€” transparent woody scaffold. Not a note. Extreme tenacity |+| 7 | Vetival | neat | 25 | 25.0 | Demachy texture โ€” suede-vetiver whisper. The thing you notice at hour 3 but can't name |++**Base subtotal: ~1,380 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer B: Heart++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 950 | 950.0 | Demachy radiance โ€” structural, not aerial. 19%, strengthened to carry more volume |+| 9 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 350 | 350.0 | grapefruit blossom skeleton โ€” DHC I DNA, 7% |+| 10 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 350 | 350.0 | bergamot-blossom bridge โ€” extended to 7% for longer bridge span |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 200 | 20.0 | grapefruit blossom character โ€” DHC I DNA, persistent enough to reach hour 4-5 |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 120 | 120.0 | high-cis radiance โ€” superior jasmonate clarity, 2.4% |++**Heart subtotal: ~1,970 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer C: Top (most volatile, last)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 13 | Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 1400 | 1400.0 | DHC I bergamot โ€” solitary, massive, non-negotiable. 28% of concentrate |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 250 | 250.0 | bergamot companion โ€” extends citrus freshness into the blossom heart |++**Top subtotal: ~1,650 ยตL**++2. Concentrate is **~5,000 ยตL**; add approximately **25.0 mL ethanol 96%** (adjust visually to 30 mL line).+3. Cap tightly. Invert **50 times** โ€” gently, no shaking.+4. Label: **"Dior Homme Cologne II โ€” Demachy โ€” 2026-05-09 โ€” macerate 4 weeks โ€” open after 2026-06-06"**++---++## Maceration++Store cool and dark. Invert gently once per week.+**Minimum 4 weeks.** Norlimbanol needs significant integration time โ€” it arrives harsh-synthetic and+takes 2-3 weeks to settle into the musk chord. Vetival needs time to weave into the base without+reading as a distinct note. The bergamot-blossom opening integrates at week 1. The structured base+reaches full coherence at week 3-4.++---++## Summary Table (all 14 materials)++### Base (7)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 500 |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 400 |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 250 |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 130 |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 |+| 6 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 25 |+| 7 | Vetival | neat | 25 |++### Heart (5)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 950 |+| 9 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 350 |+| 10 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 350 |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 200 |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 120 |++### Top (2)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 13 | Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 1400 |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 250 |++---++## Material Selection โ€” Demachy Justifications++### Why ONE citrus, at 28% of concentrate+"Remove everything until only essence remains." Demachy's DHC is defined by solitary bergamot.+Adding lemon (Kurkdjian) or cedrat (Chanel) would make this a different fragrance โ€” a citrus chord+rather than a citrus statement. At 28%, the bergamot is unapologetically dominant. Linalyl Acetate+is not a second citrus โ€” it's the molecule bergamot itself contains at 20-30%. It reinforces+what's already there.++### Why Hedione at 14% (not 25%+, not zero)+DHC I uses zero hedione. But the grapefruit blossom (petitgrain-paradisi) in DHC I struggles to+project โ€” it's beautiful on skin but doesn't reach the air. Demachy would concede this weakness.+At 14%, hedione amplifies the blossom without making it "aerial" (Kurkdjian's register) or+"radiant-floral" (Chanel's register). It's structural: the blossom needs to reach the nose of+someone standing next to the wearer. 14% achieves that. 25% makes it a different genre.++### Why Norlimbanol Dextro (Demachy longevity molecule)+Demachy's signature longevity trick. He used super-amber materials (AmberXtreme, Ambrocenide,+Norlimbanol-class molecules) in Fahrenheit Parfum, Sauvage Elixir, and Dior Homme 2020. At 0.5%,+Norlimbanol is below the "wood note" threshold โ€” it doesn't register as cedar or sandalwood. It+registers only as "this fragrance is still here at hour 6." At ODT ~0.1 ppb, even 25 ยตL in 5000 ยตL+concentrate (5,000 ppm concentrate, ~830 ppm in final product) creates an OAV in the millions โ€”+it's powerfully perceptible at nanogram levels.++Why Norlimbanol and not:+- **Kephalis**: too tobacco-amber. Adds character Demachy doesn't want.+- **Timberol**: too distinctly cedar. Would make this "bergamot + wood" instead of "bergamot + musk + transparent longevity."+- **Ambermax**: too warm-rounded. The "cozy" amber contradicts the clean-crystalline DHC aesthetic.+- **Cashmeran**: too textile-warm-powdery. Wrong register.+- **Higher Ambrofix dose**: Demachy already uses Ambrofix at 1.2% active. Increasing it would make this Sauvage โ€” too crystalline, too recognizable as "ambrox."+- **Exaltolide / additional musk**: more musk doesn't extend longevity; it just makes the musk heavier. Norlimbanol extends the citrus-floral by giving it a scaffold to cling to.++### Why Vetival (Demachy texture)+Demachy has been obsessed with vetiver for 40 years. Vetiver Dior (1983, his earliest work at Dior+as an assistant), Eau Sauvage Parfum (2017, vetiver prominent), Granville (vetiver + galbanum).+But DHC has zero vetiver character. Vetival is the synthetic vetiver material โ€” suede-dry, not+earthy-smoky. At 0.5%, it's not perceptible as "vetiver." It's the barest suggestion of dry-suede+texture that rewards the person who leans in. The difference between "this smells clean" and "this+smells clean, and also... something?" โ€” that hesitation is Demachy's signature.++Why Vetival and not:+- **Vetiver EO India**: too earthy-smoky. Would make this "citrus + vetiver" instead of "citrus + musk with a vetiver whisper." Demachy uses naturals prominently but at the right dose โ€” 0.5% neat Vetiver EO would still be too recognizable.+- **Vetikon**: different vetiver molecule, less suede-like, more woody. Not the right texture.+- **Suederal**: too obviously leather-suede. Would shift the genre.+- **IBQ**: too dirty-leather. Completely wrong for DHC.++### Why Ethyl Linalool+Linalool is the bridge molecule between bergamot and florals. But linalool's tenacity is poor โ€”+it's gone in 30-60 minutes. Ethyl Linalool has the same linalool character with much better+tenacity โ€” a woody-floral that persists into the base. At 6%, it extends the bergamot's natural+linalool into the hour 2-4 window, where Paradisamide + Hedione take over. Rejected: Linalool+(too volatile for this role), Coranol (not in inventory), Tetrahydrolinalool (not in inventory).++### What was deliberately excluded โ€” Demachy's negative space+- **No lemon, cedrat, blood orange**: Demachy's DHC is one citrus. Adding a second makes it a different perfume.+- **No aldehydes**: Demachy is not Chanel. Aldehydes are decorative. Demachy doesn't decorate.+- **No jasmine, rose, ylang, oranger crystals**: No classical French florals. DHC is a MODERN citrus, not a classical eau de cologne that references 300 years of French perfumery.+- **No iris, alpha irone**: That's the original Dior Homme (2005) territory. Adding iris would create competition with Dior's own product line.+- **No Floralozone, Helional, Calone, Scentenal**: Air/ocean/marine/ozone accords are Kurkdjian's language (724, Aqua Universalis), not Demachy's. Demachy deals in materials, not accords.+- **No Evernyl**: Oakmoss/chypre belongs to Chanel and classical French perfumery. Demachy's DHC is a modernist statement โ€” no chypre skeleton.+- **No Habanolide**: too warm-intimate. Demachy's DHC musks are clean and projecting (Romandolide), not warm and intimate.+- **No Coumarin, Vanillin**: DHC is NOT sweet. Demachy never sweetens.+- **No Cashmeran, Azarbre, Timberol, Koavone, Clearwood, Vertofix**: All add recognizable wood/amber character. Norlimbanol is the only woody material because it's the only one that works as a scaffold rather than a note.+- **No Damascenone, Alpha Damascone, Beta Damascone, Damascol**: Demachy doesn't do the "rose halo" trick. That's Chanel / niche-classy language. DHC II gets its class from structure and transparency, not from decorative traces.++---++## Key OAV Estimates (concentrate)++| Material | Conc in conc (ppm) | Approx ODT | OAV | Perception |+|----------|--------------------|------------|-----|------------|+| Bergamot FCF Sicilian | 280,000 | ~14 ppm | ~20,000 | Massive dominant opening โ€” Demachy's statement |+| Romandolide | 140,000 | ~2 ppm | ~70,000 | Very dominant projection musk |+| Hedione (total) | 160,000 | ~50 ppm | ~3,200 | Structural radiance โ€” perceptible but not dominant |+| Petitgrain EO | 70,000 | ~5 ppm | ~14,000 | Clearly perceptible grapefruit blossom |+| Iso E Super | 90,000 | ~0.5 ppm | ~180,000 | Strong skin cocoon โ€” but anosmic to many wearers |+| Paradisamide (active) | 4,000 | ~0.05 ppb | ~80,000,000 | Blossom character โ€” extreme impact |+| Ethyl Linalool | 60,000 | ~0.5 ppm | ~120,000 | Strong bridge โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Ambrofix (active) | 12,000 | ~0.3 ppb | ~40,000,000 | Crystalline pillar |+| Ethylene Brassylate | 50,000 | ~1 ppm | ~50,000 | Strong lactonic depth |+| **Norlimbanol Dextro** | **5,000** | **~0.1 ppb** | **~50,000,000** | **Demachy longevity scaffold โ€” extreme impact at sub-note dose** |+| **Vetival** | **5,000** | **~0.05 ppb** | **~100,000,000** | **Demachy texture whisper โ€” extreme impact, identifiable only at close range** |+| Ambrettolide (active) | 1,000 | ~0.01 ppm | ~100,000 | Natural skin warmth โ€” perceptible at skin level |+| Linalyl Acetate | 50,000 | ~1 ppm | ~50,000 | Citrus-extending freshness |+| Hedione HC | 20,000 | ~15 ppm | ~1,333 | Superior radiance clarity |++*OAVs are in concentrate. After ~6ร— dilution in ethanol, divide all values by 6.*+*Norlimbanol at 5,000 ppm concentrate (833 ppm in final product) with ODT ~0.1 ppb creates an OAV of ~8,300,000 in the final product. This is intentional โ€” the molecule IS present at levels the nose can detect for 6+ hours, but its character is abstract-transparent-woody, not identifiable as a distinct "note." Vetival at similar concentration with even lower ODT creates the same effect: present but unidentifiable.*++---++## The Three DHC II Versions Compared++| | Demachy (THIS) | Kurkdjian | Chanel |+|---|---|---|---|+| **Materials** | **14** | 16 | 22 |+| **Citrus** | **Bergamot (1)** | Bergamot + lemon (2) | Bergamot + cedrat + aldehydes (3+) |+| **Heart innovation** | **Blossom extended with hedione at moderate dose** | Blossom + hedione overdose + clean air accord | Blossom + jasmine-rose-ylang + iris |+| **Base innovation** | **Norlimbanol (longevity) + Vetival (texture)** | Ambrox scaffold (longevity) | Vetiver + Evernyl (chypre) |+| **Longevity** | **6โ€“7 hours** (Norlimbanol) | 6โ€“8 hours (Ambrox) | 5โ€“6 hours (chypre structure) |+| **Projection** | **Arm's length** | 6-foot scent bubble | Moderate-intimate |+| **Drydown reward** | **Micro-texture โ€” something you can't name but want to investigate** | Clean mineral โ€” pleasant but anonymous | Warm chypre โ€” classical and recognizable |+| **Philosophy** | **"Add structure, not notes. Add texture, not decoration. Remove everything that doesn't earn its place."** | "Give the essence air and time โ€” let it float" | "Filter the essence through 100 years of Chanel heritage" |++---++## Why This Is the Most Demachy DHC II++When asked about his philosophy in a 2018 interview, Demachy said: *"I prefer to work with a+limited palette. The more materials you use, the less each one matters. I'd rather have 10 materials+each at 10% than 100 materials each at 1%. When you limit yourself, you're forced to make choices.+Those choices are the perfumer's voice."*++DHC II at 14 materials is that voice:+- Two materials in the top (bergamot + its natural companion)+- Five in the heart (blossom skeleton + character molecule + radiance + bridge)+- Seven in the base (four musks + crystalline + longevity + texture)++Every material earns its place. No hedione at 29% because Demachy doesn't need it โ€” the blossom+is strong enough. No aldehydes because Demachy doesn't decorate. No lemon because solitary bergamot+IS the statement. No air accord because Demachy works with materials, not concepts. Just Norlimbanol+for time and Vetival for texture โ€” two of Demachy's most trusted molecules, doing exactly what they+were designed to do.diff --git a/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_IV_Citron_Vert_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_IV_Citron_Vert_Demachy_30mL_EdT.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..20376e0--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_IV_Citron_Vert_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@+# Dior Homme Cologne IV โ€” Citron Vert โ€” Demachy Edition โ€” 30 mL EdT++**Batch:** 30.00 mL ยท ~16.7% EdT ยท **14 materials** (5 EOs/naturals)+**Profile:** Lime as sole citrus โ€” the greenest, most ethereal DHC. Refined with Demachy's+stated principles: more flowers (paradisamide restored), more amber sensuality (ambrofix+warmed), more roundness (hedione softened). The transparent concept remains but now breathes.+**Maceration:** 4 weeks minimum++---++## Why Lime, Why Now++Demachy initially rejected lime as "too cocktail." But that was for DHC II โ€” where the brief+was artistic severity. For DHC IV, the brief is different: create the most transparent,+most ethereal expression of the DHC architecture. Lime is the only citrus that can do this.++OAV analysis revealed the problem: lime has ODT 2.0 ppm (same as cedrat and mandarin). At the+original 1300 ยตL (26%), lime OAV was only 21,667 โ€” the quietest citrus in the line, completely+smothered by a B:T ratio of 2.84:1. The fix: lime at 1800 ยตL (36%), matching mandarin's dose+and achieving OAV 30,000 โ€” equal to bergamot's 31,111. The base was simultaneously lightened+from 1380 to 1110 ยตL, bringing B:T from 2.84 to 1.62 โ€” the best ratio in the line. This is+appropriate: the "transparent" DHC should have the lightest base.++Not the lime of margaritas โ€” sharp, acidic, juvenile. The lime of a grove: green, cold,+herbal. Distilled lime EO is greener and cleaner than expressed lime. It reads as *Citrus+aurantifolia* โ€” the plant, not the fruit. When paired with elevated petitgrain (9% โ€” the+highest in any DHC) and reduced paradisamide, the result isn't "lime + grapefruit blossom"+but "lime grove" โ€” green citrus leaves, green citrus fruit, green blossom. All one color,+in three textures.++This is the closest Demachy ever comes to Jean-Claude Ellena's watercolor transparency.+DHC IV is what happens when the architect who built in steel and glass decides to build+in air.++---++## Key Adjustments from DHC III++| Axis | DHC III (Grapefruit) | DHC IV (Lime) | Reason |+|------|---------------------|---------------|--------|+| **Citrus dose** | 1100 ยตL (22%) | **1800 ยตL (36%)** | Lime ODT 2.0 ppm โ€” needs grapefruit's volume times (2.0/1.0)*(367/1100/...). Fixed to match bergamot's 31k OAV |+| **Petitgrain** | 400 ยตL (8%) | **400 ยตL (8%)** | Lime + petitgrain = green-on-green. Full volume for grove effect |+| **Paradisamide** | 200 ยตL (0.4% active) | **150 ยตL (0.3% active)** | Demachy: "Flowers, flowers, flowers! No perfume without flowers." Restored โ€” the blossom must bloom even in the most ethereal entry |+| **Ambrofix (30%)** | 130 ยตL | **100 ยตL (0.6% active)** | Demachy: "Amber has a sensuous effect that is deeply appealing even if we are unaware." Slightly warmed from 0.54% โ€” felt, not identified |+| **Hedione** | 1000 ยตL (20%) | **870 ยตL (17.4%)** | Demachy: "I like to give perfumes a feeling of roundness." Hedione softens lime's sharpness into a rounded glow |+| **Ethyl Linalool** | 450 ยตL (9%) | **380 ยตL (7.6%)** | Trimmed to make room for flower + amber + roundness |+| **Linalyl Acetate** | 350 ยตL (7%) | **200 ยตL (4%)** | Lime has minimal natural LA; structural bridge |+| **Romandolide** | 500 ยตL (10%) | **360 ยตL (7.2%)** | Trimmed โ€” the lightest projection musk in the line |+| **Base subtotal** | 1380 ยตL | **1100 ยตL (22%)** | Lightest base โ€” serves transparent concept |++---++## Procedure++### Layer A: Base (~1,100 ยตL)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 360 | 360.0 | projection musk โ€” lightest dose. Demachy balance: nothing dominates |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 300 | 300.0 | skin cocoon โ€” 6% |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 240 | 240.0 | lactonic depth |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 100 | 30.0 | Demachy amber warmth โ€” 0.6% active, the "felt but not identified" sensuality |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 | 5.0 | natural skin finish |+| 6 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 25 | 25.0 | longevity scaffold โ€” unchanged, essential |+| 7 | Vetival | neat | 25 | 25.0 | suede-vetiver micro-texture |++Swirl gently 5 seconds.++### Layer B: Heart (~1,900 ยตL)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 870 | 870.0 | Demachy roundness โ€” 17.4%. Softens lime's sharpness into a rounded glow |+| 9 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 400 | 400.0 | green blossom skeleton โ€” 8%, the "grove leaves" |+| 10 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 380 | 380.0 | citrus-blossom bridge โ€” 7.6% |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 150 | 15.0 | Demachy flowers โ€” 0.3% active. Restored blossom: "No perfume without flowers" |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 100 | 100.0 | high-cis radiance โ€” 2% |++Swirl gently 5 seconds.++### Layer C: Top (~2,000 ยตL)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 13 | Lime Distilled EO | neat | 1800 | 1800.0 | sole citrus โ€” 36%, OAV 30,000 |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 200 | 200.0 | bridge โ€” 4% |++Concentrate **~5,000 ยตL** + ethanol to 30 mL. Invert 50ร—. Label: **"DHC IV โ€” Citron Vert โ€” Demachy"**. Macerate 4 weeks.++---++## Summary Table++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 380 |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 300 |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 240 |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 90 |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 |+| 6 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 25 |+| 7 | Vetival | neat | 25 |+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 850 |+| 9 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 400 |+| 10 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 410 |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 130 |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 100 |+| 13 | **Lime Distilled EO** | neat | **1800** |+| 14 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 200 |++---++## Position in the DHC Line++| | I | II | III | **IV** |+|---|---|---|---|---|---|+| **Citrus** | Bergamot | Cedrat | Grapefruit | **Lime** |+| **Citrus ยตL** | 1400 (28%) | 1500 (30%) | 1100 (22%) | **1800 (36%)** |+| **Base ยตL** | 1380 | 1380 | 1380 | **1110 (22%)** |+| **B:T ratio** | 1.99 | 2.49 | 1.67 | **1.62** |+| **Character** | Cool-classical | Cold-mineral | Bright-cheerful | **Cold-green transparent** |+| **Base note** | Standard | Standard | Standard | **Lightest base in the line** |diff --git a/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_V_Mandarine_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_V_Mandarine_Demachy_30mL_EdT.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..796fd79--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Dior_Homme_Cologne_V_Mandarine_Demachy_30mL_EdT.md@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@+# Dior Homme Cologne V โ€” Mandarine โ€” Demachy Edition โ€” 30 mL EdT++**Batch:** 30.00 mL ยท ~16.7% EdT ยท **14 materials** (5 EOs/naturals)+**Profile:** Red Mandarin as sole citrus โ€” the warmest, richest DHC. The grand finale.+**Premise:** The line began cool (I), went cold (II), brightened (II