-Irone active 3.14 % = **3.82 % combined iris-rhizome signal** (fatty-acid-to-irone ratio 0.22 vs natural orris butter's ~8 โ€” our composition is intentionally irone-dominant for a "silver iris" character rather than a "butter iris" one; Myristic provides the *texture cue*, not the full butter character)+- **Macrocyclic musk chord active mass** (Habanolide neat 150 + EB neat 432 + Ambrettolide 10 % 36.4 + Musk Ketone 10 % 21.4) = **639.8 ยตL active = 9.69 %** of concentrate++### Why Myristic Acid and not more musk++Exaltolide's role in the original v7 was **not just musk** โ€” it was *also* an orris-butter texture cue. Replacing it with additional macrocyclic musk alone (v7ยทiยทhab) would over-weight the musk chord and still leave the orris-butter-texture register empty. **Myristic Acid is the canonical orris-butter molecule** (~85 % of natural orris butter's non-volatile mass). At 0.68 % it sits inside the orris-butter-texture window used by classical iris soliflores and modern Infusion-style compositions โ€” enough to register as *"creamy fatty iris skin"* on the nose, not enough to read as cold-cream soap (โฅ 1 % flattens iris shimmer). This is the character-correct substitution.++### Myristic Acid โ€” Not Optional++Unlike the v7ยทiยทhab draft (which treated Myristic as an experimental sidebar), v7ยทiยทm makes Myristic **canonical** because the perfumery target of the Exaltolide line was orris-butter texture, not just musk. Skipping Myristic here would leave the composition reading as an "iris without the butter" โ€” scorer-good but perfumer-thin. If you specifically want a *non-butter* silver iris (as in Iris Silver Mist's approach), omit Myristic and reduce Ebanol by 100 ยตL โ€” but that is a different brief from *Luxe Lactรฉe*, which is explicitly a **lactonic-creamy-butter** iris.++## Maceration & Bottling Protocol++1. **Weigh the beaker empty.** Tare.+2. **Pre-dispense B1 (Ebanol 740 ยตL) and B2 (Hexyl Salicylate 612 ยตL) FIRST.** Place the beaker in a 40 ยฐC water bath (fill a larger vessel with hot tap water at 40โ€“45 ยฐC). **Weigh 45 mg Myristic Acid Powder on analytical balance** (record to 0.1 mg precision; accept ยฑ2 mg tolerance) and add it to the warm Ebanol+Hexyl Sal mass. Swirl for 3โ€“5 min until Myristic is fully dissolved (no visible particles; solution remains clear or slightly opalescent). This is the **orris-butter pre-dissolution step** and must be completed before any other base material is added โ€” Myristic dissolves cleanly in the warm lipophilic base but clumps in cold dilutions.+3. **Remove from water bath, cool 2 min to ~30 ยฐC**, then **dispense remaining Section A (Base)** in order B3โ’B8. Use P1000 (100โ€“1000 ยตL) for EB/Ambrettolide/Ambrofix; P200 for Coumarin/Musk Ketone/Habanolide. **Habanolide (B8) LAST in base โ€” neat, high-impact macrocyclic; dispense slowly and let it stream into the liquid mass, not onto the beaker wall. Triple-rinse the pipette tip in clean DPG after.** Rinse pipette tips between dilution-tier changes.+4. **Swirl 60 s.** Verify Musk Ketone and Coumarin crystals are dissolving (should be no visible granules after 5 min โ€” if any remain, add 200 ยตL neat DPG as extra solvent and note it). Verify Myristic remains dissolved (should show no recrystallisation at 30 ยฐC with the full base mass present).+4. **Dispense Section B (Heart)** in order H1โ’H17. **Critical steps:**+   - H1 (ฮฑ-Irone 30 %) is viscous โ€” draw slowly, dispense slowly.+   - H16 (Indole 10 %) โ€” positive-displacement pipette only; Indole is a powerful-trace material, contamination risk; rinse tip 3ร— in clean DPG after use.+   - H17 (ฮฒ-Ionone) last in heart โ€” it's neat and volatile-adjacent.+5. **Swirl 60 s.** Solution should be pale amber, slightly viscous, fully homogeneous.+6. **Dispense Section C (Top)** in order T1โ’T6 rapidly (< 2 min). **T6 Geosmin (1 %) is the LAST drop โ€” 1.8 ยตL, use P10 positive displacement, one single drop.**+7. **Transfer** the 6.60 mL concentrate to a 50 mL