n. Just enough to be heard. Never enough to be noticed." |+| 18 | **Scentenal** | 1% in DPG | 0.50 | "The dream. Not a note โ€” an atmosphere. You smell it and think of film grain, cathedral stone, the haze after rain. It is the question the perfume asks. I doubled it because I trust this molecule more than any other." |++### What Ellena cut++| Cut | Why |+|---|---|+| Orivone, Ultralia | One iris molecule is enough. Support is apology. |+| Mayol, Nympheal | Muguet is a memory. Perfume is the present. |+| PEA, Geraniol, Damascol, Rose Oxide | Rose doesn't belong in a lullaby. Rose is for seduction. |+| DBCA | White-floral cosmetic is weight. This is watercolor. |+| Iso E Super | The cocoon is heavy. Transparency is light. |+| Azarbre, Vertofix, Polysantol | No woods. No structure. A lullaby floats. |+| Exaltolide, Ambrettolide | Two musks are enough. Five musks are a concert. This is a song. |+| Costus Olifac | Warm-skin is too intimate. I want the wearer to feel alone, not accompanied. |+| Siam Benzoin | Balsamic is ancient. This is modern. |++### 50 mL EDP Weighing Sheet++| # | Ingredient | Weigh (g) |+|---|-----------|----------:|+| 1 | Bergamot Sicilian | 0.550 |+| 2 | Red Mandarin EO | 0.330 |+| 3 | Aldehyde C11 undecylenic | 0.033 |+| 4 | Aldehyde C12 MNA (1% in DPG) | 0.275 |+| 5 | Heliotropal | 0.660 |+| 6 | Anisaldehyde | 0.330 |+| 7 | Coumarin (20% in DPG) | 0.825 |+| 8 | Vanillin (10% in DPG) | 0.440 |+| 9 | Alpha Irone (30% in DEP) | 0.880 |+| 10 | Hedione | 1.650 |+| 11 | Benzyl Acetate | 0.220 |+| 12 | Farnesol | 0.028 |+| 13 | Ethyl Maltol (10% in DPG) | 0.275 |+| 14 | Cashmeran (20% in DPG) | 0.660 |+| 15 | Musk Ketone (10% in DPG) | 0.660 |+| 16 | Ethylene Brassylate | 0.550 |+| 17 | Romandolide | 0.330 |+| 18 | Scentenal (1% in DPG) | 0.055 |++Concentrate ~8.2 g. Ethanol 96% to 50 mL. Same maceration.++### Compounding++**Base:** EB โ’ Romandolide โ’ Cashmeran 20% โ’ Musk Ketone 10% โ’ Scentenal 1%. Swirl.++**Heart:** Hedione โ’ Iris (Alpha Irone 30%). Swirl. โ’ Powder jingle (Heliotropal warm if solid โ’ Anisaldehyde โ’ Coumarin 20% โ’ Vanillin 10% โ’ Ethyl Maltol 10%). Swirl. โ’ Farnesol โ’ Benzyl Acetate. Swirl.++**Top:** Bergamot Sicilian โ’ Red Mandarin โ’ C12 MNA 1% โ’ C11 undecylenic. Cap.++### Ellena's verdict++"It is 18 materials. You could do it in 15. The Ethyl Maltol is sentimental. The Farnesol is apology. The Benzyl Acetate could be silence. But I accept 18 because the aldehydic top is irreplaceable and the powder jingle is honest. The Scentenal makes it mine. The single iris makes it yours. The Cashmeran at 6% is the exact weight of a yellow blanket. Not 10% โ€” that's a duvet. 6% is cashmere you can see through."++"Jean-Claude โ€” you just described my formula to me."++---++## VARIANT โ€” Givaudan Edition (27 materials ยท clean transparency)++**Philosophy:** A Givaudan perfumer thinks in captives. They have two showpiece molecules available here: **Nympheal** (muguet radiance โ€” already in the formula) and **Ambrofix** (clean modern amber โ€” not yet used). Their aesthetic is modern, transparent, almost tech-forward. They'd never use 1950s cedar-amber (Azarbre) when Ambrofix is available. They'd never use Mayol when Nympheal is in the same formula. They'd boost Hedione because radiance IS modern perfumery. They'd add Paradisamide at trace because fruit-ghost amplification is signature Givaudan technique, regardless of which competitor's patent expired on it.++### What Givaudan changes++| Change | From | To | Why |+|---|---:|---:|---|+| **Amber warmth** | Azarbre 2% | **Ambrofix 30% ยท 4%** | Clean modern amber replaces cedar-amber. Ambrofix is Givaudan's signature captive โ€” mineral, transparent, weightless warmth |+| **Muguet** | Mayol 1% | **removed** | Nympheal is the better muguet. One Givaudan muguet is enough |+| **Radiance** | Hedione 15% | **Hedione 22%** | Maximum radiance. This is Givaudan's philosophy โ€” projection through transparency |+| **Fixative** | Vertofix 2% | **removed** | Redundant with EB + Iso E + Ambrofix |+| **Fruit ghost** | none | **Paradisamide 10% ยท 15 ยตL** | Amplifies the lactonic jingle. The Gamma Undecalactone peach gets a tropical ghost that the wearer can't name |+| **Diffusion** | DBCA 1.50% | **DBCA 1.50% (kept)** | DBCA stays โ€” gardenia-rose cosmetic is the right white-floral register |++### Modified formula (changes only โ€” rest stays as main)++**HEART โ€” Jasmine Body** (unchanged)+| # | Ingredient | Dilution | mass_frac (%) |+|---|-----------|----------|----------:|+| 5 | DBCA | neat | 1.50 |++**HEART โ€” Muguet Memory** (remade)+| # | Ingredient | Dilution | mass_frac (%) |+|---|-----------|----------|----------:|+| 14 | Nympheal | neat | **0.80** | Boosted from 0.50% โ€” Givaudan trusts their own molecule more |++*Mayol dropped.*++**HEART โ€” Radiance** (boosted)+| # | Ingredient | Dilution | mass_frac (%) |+|---|-----------|----------|----------:|+| 20 | Hedione | neat | **22.00** | Up from 15% โ€” maximum radiance |++**BASE โ€” Warmth** (Azarbre out, Ambrofix in)+| # | Ingredient | Dilution | mass_frac (%) |+|---|-----------|----------|----------:|+| 30 | **Ambrofix** | 30% w/v | 4.00 | Clean mineral-transparent amber. Replaces Azarbre |++*Vertofix dropped. Azarbre dropped.*++**BASE โ€” Fruit Ghost** (new)++| # | Ingredient | Dilution | mass_frac (%) |+|---|-----------|----------|----------:|+| 34 | **Paradisamide** | 10% in DPG | 0.15 | Fruit-ghost amplification. OAV < 5 โ€” subliminal tropical shimmer behind the lactonic jingle |++### Givaudan perfumer's notes++"Cashmeran at 10% is the correct dose. Iso E Super at 4% is the correct dose. Hexyl Salicylate over Benzyl Salicylate is the correct choice โ€” transparency over cosmetic weight. Musk Ketone at 6% is bold but correct โ€” only a nitro-musk gives you 1950s talc. Exaltolide for skin-fat depth โ€” Laurent (Le Guernec) would approve."++"The additions are minimal: Ambrofix for modernization, Paradisamide for the fruit-ghost the jingle always needed, Hedione at 22% because radiance shouldn't whisper. The cuts are obvious: Mayol is redundant when Nympheal is present. Vertofix is redundant when EB + Iso E + Ambrofix form the base. Azarbre is cedar-amber โ€” this is 1950s, not 1850s."++"The formula is correct. It was correct before we arrived. We are not rebuilding โ€” we are finishing."++**27 materials.** Top signature preserved. Iris veil preserved. Aldehydes untouched.++---++## VARIANT โ€” Ropion Edition (Malle ยท maximalist ยท 40 materials)++**Philosophy:** "A perfume should be HEARD. Not all perfume is intimate โ€” some perfume is a room you enter." Ropion never cuts. He adds. Every existing material stays. His additions stack on top.++| Change | From | To | Why |+|---|---|---|+| **C11 undecylenic** | 0.30% | 0.60% | Double the aldehydic star. Chanel No. 5 territory |+| **Heliotropal** | 6.00% | 8.00% | The jingle should be undeniable |+| **Hedione** | 15.00% | 20.00% | Radiance at maximum volume |+| **Cashmeran 20%** | 10.00% | 12.00% | The blanket is a duvet |+| **Musk Ketone 10%** | 6.00% | 8.00% | The era signal at full volume |+| **Costus Olifac 10%** | 0.25% | 0.40% | Warm-skin is a presence, not a whisper |+| **ADD Labdanum Absolute 10%** | โ€” | 2.00% | Amber depth under the blanket. Ropion's signature warmth |+| **ADD Kephalis** | โ€” | 0.50% | Woody-amber power. Architecture, not suggestion |+| **ADD Galbanum Resinoid 10%** | โ€” | 0.10% | Green-sharp aldehydic companion. Ropion loves a "crack" in the opening |+| **ADD Exaltolide 10%** | 1.00% (already present) | kept | Keep the 5th musk |++**Top changes only:** C11 doubled. C12 MNA stays. Galbanum 10% at 10 ยตL added โ€” "the aldehydic lipstick needs a green crack. Not green in the heart. Green in the opening. Like a perfume that knows it's perfume." The C11-C12-Galbanum top is now a 3-body aldehydic.++"Dominique โ€” you just made the lullaby louder than the film."++"The film IS loud. Technicolor. Widescreen. You think 1950s cinema whispers?"++---++## VARIANT โ€” Wasser Edition (Guerlain ยท 33 materials)++**Philosophy:** "This is Guerlinade. Heliotropal + Coumarin + Vanillin is OUR accord. Let me show you how it's done."++Wasser recognizes the powder jingle as Guerlain's house signature โ€” the accord that defined L'Heure Bleue, Shalimar, and Aprรจs l'Ondรฉe. He doesn't change the structure. He deepens it.++| Change | From | To | Why |+|---|---|---|+| **Vanillin 10%** | 4.00% | drop | Ethyl Vanillin replaces it โ€” darker, more complex. "Vanillin is for cake. Ethyl Vanillin is for Guerlain." |+| **ADD Ethyl Vanillin** | โ€” | 0.50% neat | The Guerlain vanilla. Richer, deeper, 3ร— more potent |+| **Siam Benzoin 50%** | 1.00% | 3.00% | Full Guerlain balsamic base. The 8-hour whisper becomes an 8-hour presence |+| **ADD Tonka Bean FO** | โ€” | 1.00% | Richer coumarinic body under the Coumarin. "Guerlinade isn't four molecules. It's five." |+| **Heliotropal** | 6.00% | 7.00% | More powder. Guerlain's DNA is powder-first |+| **ADD Labdanum Absolute 10%** | โ€” | 0.80% | Guerlain's amber โ€” the warm-resinous bridge between jingle and blanket |+| **DROP Costus Olifac** | 0.25% | removed | "Animalic skin is for Lutens. Guerlain is for skin that's already warm." |+| **DROP Scentenal** | 0.10% | removed | "Mineral haze is for Ellena. Guerlain doesn't do haze. Guerlain does presence." |++"Thierry โ€” you just made my lullaby a Shalimar flanker."++"No. I made your lullaby a Guerlain. You were already 80% there. You just didn't know what you were quoting."++---++## VARIANT โ€” Nicolai Edition (conservative ยท 33 materials)++**Philosophy:** "The formula is correct. I change three things. Maybe four."++Nicolai is Patricia de Nicolai โ€” Guerlain granddaughter, Osmothรจque director, trained perfumer who believes classic structure is correct until proven otherwise. She doesn't add captives, doesn't chase trends, doesn't cut for minimalism.++| Change | From | To | Why |+|---|---|---|+| **Damascol 10%** | 1.00% | drop | "Damascone esters are 1990s. This is 1950s." |+| **ADD PEA** | โ€” | 1.50% neat | "Classical rose petal. Damascol is plum blush โ€” a modern idea of rose. PEA is what rose actually smelled like in 1950." |+| **Siam Benzoin 50%** | 1.00% | 2.00% | "One percent is a whisper. Two percent is a presence. Three percent is Guerlain โ€” and I'm not Guerlain." |+| **DROP Rose Oxide 10%** | 0.15% | removed | "Rose Oxide is metallic. Rose in a lullaby shouldn't clang." |+| **DROP Geraniol** | 0.50% | dropped | "Geraniol is rose brightness. The rose in this perfume should be soft โ€” PEA alone is correct." |+| **DROP Exaltolide 10%** | 1.00% | removed | "Four musk chord. Five is excessive. Four is classical." |+| **DROP DBCA** | 1.50% | removed | "Gardenia is not jasmine. You used a gardenia molecule for jasmine diffusion. Use Benzyl Acetate at 2% โ€” it's the correct molecule for jasmine hum in a classical formula." |+| **ADD Benzyl Acetate** | โ€” | 2.00% | "There. Jasmine diffusion, classical molecule, correct dose." |+| **Nympheal** | 0.50% | removed | "Nympheal is Givaudan's molecule. Use Hydroxycitronellal at 0.70% โ€” it's the classical muguet. You don't need a captive for a lullaby." |+| **ADD Hydroxycitronellal** | โ€” | 0.70% | Classical dewy muguet |++"This is the formula a 1950s perfumer would have written. The aldehydic top. The powder jingle. One iris. Classical rose. Classical muguet. Four musks. It's not fashionable โ€” it's correct."++33 materials. Top signature preserved at original 1950s doses (C11 at 0.30%, no doubling like Ropion). Every molecule period-appropriate. No captives. No modern materials. Just the perfume your formula was always trying to be.++---++## VARIANT โ€” Le Labo (12 materials ยท minimalist ยท "SAND 26")++**Philosophy:** "Fewer materials, not more. One molecule per role. Name it like a lab sample. Charge $320."++Le Labo doesn't build symphonies. They build haikus. The aldehydic top is 4 materials โ€” keep it. The powder jingle is 4 materials โ€” keep it. Everything else: ONE of each.++| Role | Pick | Why |+|---|---|---|+| Aldehydic top | Bergamot Sicilian + Mandarin + C11 + C12 | Preserved. The signature. |+| Powder jingle | Heliotropal + Anisaldehyde + Coumarin + Vanillin | Preserved. The core. |+| Iris | Alpha Irone 30% (8%) | One iris. No support. |+| Radiance | Hedione (18%) | Transparency. No Benzyl Acetate โ€” redundant with the aldehydes. |+| Musk | Romandolide (4%) | One musk. Projection only. EB's creaminess, MK's talc, Ambrettolide's skin โ€” all cut. One musk is the aesthetic. |+| Blanket | Cashmeran 20% (12%) | The yellow blanket at full volume. The ONLY warmth material. |+| Fixative | Hexyl Salicylate (8%) | Invisible film. |+| Dream | Scentenal 1% (0.50%) | Boosted. The "lab sample" molecule โ€” it's what makes this Le Labo instead of anyone else. |++"12 materials. 4 for the top, 4 for the heart, 4 for the base. The aldehydic-lipstick opening is your concept. The powder jingle is your architecture. The Scentenal haze is your signature. Everything else was noise."++"You just cut my perfume by two-thirds."++"I made it a Le Labo. Want it back? Add the other 23 materials. But you won't. Once you smell 12, you'll never want 35 again."++---++## VARIANT โ€” Lutens (32 materials ยท warm-amber ยท "Nocturne in Yellow")++**Philosophy:** "A lullaby isn't just soft. A lullaby is the dark that makes you want to be held." Lutens doesn't do clean animalic. He does WARM amber-dark โ€” clove, labdanum, benzoin, musk. The perfume becomes richer, heavier, more enveloping. Not fecal. Not challenging. Just DEEPER.++| Change | From | To | Why |+|---|---|---|+| **Musk Ketone 10%** | 6.00% | 10.00% | The nitro-musk that defined his Iris Silver Mist. Full volume |+| **ADD Labdanum Absolute 10%** | โ€” | 1.50% | Dark amber warmth. "The shoulder you fall asleep on is warm, not ambient." |+| **Siam Benzoin 50%** | 1.00% | 2.50% | Sweet-resinous depth. Benzoin is the original 1950s fixative |+| **ADD Eugenol*