osophy:** "Iris is Dior. Leather is Dior. Amber is Dior. You have all three in this formula but none of them speak." Demachy centers the iris, adds leather for the cinema-seat, and builds an amber base under the blanket. The lullaby becomes richer, more complex, more Dior.++| Change | From | To | Why |+|---|---|---|+| **Alpha Irone 30%** | 8.00% | 12.00% | "Iris is Dior. Dior Homme is iris. Dior Homme Parfum is iris. Your iris is quiet. Dior's iris leads." |+| **ADD Labdanum Absolute 10%** | โ€” | 2.50% | "Amber depth. Dior's base is always amber." |+| **ADD Suederal 10%** | โ€” | 40 ยตL | "The cinema seat IS leather. You had no leather. Dior adds it." |+| **ADD Evernyl** | โ€” | 0.30% | "Oakmoss. Modern replacement. Dior Homme 2020 has it. So does your lullaby now." |+| **Costus Olifac 10%** | 0.25% | 0.35% | "Skin warmth. Dior loves a lived-in note. Boosted from your trace." |+| **Cashmeran 20%** | 10.00% | 12.00% | "The blanket at Dior volume." |+| **Musk Ketone 10%** | 6.00% | 8.00% | Louder era signal |+| **Hedione** | 15.00% | kept | "Correct dose. Demachy doesn't overdose Hedione." |+| **DROP Scentenal** | 0.10% | kept | "Actually โ€” keep it. Dior uses atmospheric molecules. Fahrenheit has violet leaf. Sauvage has ambroxan haze. Scentenal is your atmospheric. Keep 0.15%." |+| **ADD Iso E Super** | 4.00% | kept | "Demachy uses it. Dior Homme is built on it. Keep the cocoon." |+| **Nympheal** | 0.50% | kept | "Muguet is Dior's white flower. J'adore is muguet. Keep it." |+| **DROP Rose Oxide** | 0.15% | removed | "Metallic rose is Prada. Not Dior." |++*Kept entire aldehydic top (preserved). Kept powder jingle (Heliotropal 6%, Anisaldehyde 3%, Coumarin 7.50%, Vanillin 4%). Kept DBCA 1.50%, Mayol 1%, PEA 1%, Geraniol 0.50%, Damascol 1%, Farnesol 0.25%, EB 9%, Ambrettolide 3.50%, Romandolide 2%, Exaltolide 1%, Hexyl Salicylate 8%, Siam Benzoin 1%, Polysantol 0.50%, Azarbre 2%, Vertofix 2%.*++33 materials. The formula now has leather (Suederal), amber (Labdanum), and maximal iris. Dior's three signatures. The lullaby is now Homme.++---++## VARIANT โ€” YSL (31 materials ยท bold aldehydic ยท "Rive Gauche Lullaby")++**Philosophy:** "YSL doesn't do quiet. Rive Gauche is the aldehydic floral that modernized Chanel. Opium is the oriental that scared Guerlain. If you want a lullaby, make it a lullaby for adults." YSL boosts everything sharp, bright, and confident. The aldehydes lead. The spice comes through. The base is clean-white-musk projection. No amber. No leather. Just radiant aldehydic confidence.++| Change | From | To | Why |+|---|---|---|+| **C11 undecylenic** | 0.30% | 0.70% | "More than Ropion. YSL aldehydes define the wearer." |+| **C12 MNA 1%** | 2.50% | 4.00% | "Double the sparkle. Rive Gauche sparkles." |+| **Hedione** | 15.00% | 22.00% | "Max radiance. YSL perfumes project. They don't sit." |+| **ADD Cardamom EO** | โ€” | 60 ยตL | "Bright spice in the opening. YSL loves a sharp top note." |+| **ADD Eugenol** | โ€” | 0.25% | "Clove warmth. Opium's signature spice. Just a trace under the aldehydes." |+| **Romandolide** | 2.00% | 4.00% | "Projection musk at double. YSL perfumes are heard." |+| **ADD Habanolide** | โ€” | 3.00% | "Clean white musk. YSL's signature 1990s base. Rive Gauche pour Homme territory." |+| **Exaltolide 10%** | 1.00% | kept | "Skin-fat depth. With Habanolide + Romandolide, this is now a 6-musk YSL chord." |+| **DROP Costus Olifac** | 0.25% | removed | "YSL doesn't do animalic-warm. YSL does sharp and clean." |+| **DROP Scentenal** | 0.10% | removed | "Atmospheric is Dior. YSL is radiant, not atmospheric." |+| **DROP Nympheal, Mayol** | โ€” | removed | "Muguet is too soft for YSL. The aldehydes are the heart." |+| **DROP Rose Oxide** | 0.15% | removed | Not YSL |+| **DROP Ethyl Maltol** | 2.50% | 1.50% | "Cotton candy is too sweet. YSL's sweet is spicy-sweet, not candy-sweet." |++*Kept: Bergamot Sicilian 5%, Red Mandarin 3%, Heliotropal 6%, Anisaldehyde 3%, Coumarin 7.50%, Vanillin 4%, Alpha Irone 8