16 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 290 | 290.0 | bergamot companion โ€” extends citrus freshness into heart |+| 17 | Aldehyde C10 | 1% | 40 | 0.4 | invisible champagne sparkle โ€” below aldehyde threshold |+| 18 | Cardamom EO | neat | 35 | 35.0 | micro-aromatic lift โ€” prevents single-dimensional citrus |++**Top subtotal: ~1,465 ยตL**++2. Concentrate is **~5,000 ยตL**; add approximately **25.0 mL ethanol 96%** (adjust visually to 30 mL line).+3. Cap tightly. Invert **50 times** โ€” gently, no shaking.+4. Label: **"Seuil du Jour โ€” v3 Classique โ€” 2026-05-09 โ€” macerate 3 weeks โ€” open after 2026-05-30"**++---++## Maceration++Store cool and dark. Invert gently once per week.+**Minimum 3 weeks.** Longer than v2 because Damascenone (Schiff base formation with Hedione),+Alpha Irone, and Ambrettolide need integration time. The bergamot softens at 1 week.+The blossom heart blooms at 2 weeks. The iris-musk base reaches full integration at 3 weeks.++---++## Summary Table (all 18 materials)++### Base (7)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 650 |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 400 |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 250 |+| 4 | Ambrofix | 30% | 150 |+| 5 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 60 |+| 6 | Ebanol | neat | 30 |+| 7 | Alpha Irone | 30% in DEP | 10 |++### Heart (7)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 8 | Hedione | neat | 1050 |+| 9 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 300 |+| 10 | Ethyl Linalool | neat | 250 |+| 11 | Paradisamide | 10% | 200 |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 100 |+| 13 | Oranger Crystals | 10% in DPG | 60 |+| 14 | Damascenone | 1% | 25 |++### Top (4)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 15 | Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 1100 |+| 16 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 290 |+| 17 | Aldehyde C10 | 1% | 40 |+| 18 | Cardamom EO | neat | 35 |++---++## Material Selection โ€” Classiness Justifications++### Why Aldehyde C10 at 0.0008% active+This is the single most impactful classiness upgrade. At this dose, Aldehyde C10 is imperceptible+as a "note" โ€” it doesn't smell like Chanel No. 5 or classical aldehydic fragrances. It functions+as a pure volatility enhancer: it lifts the bergamot opening into a champagne effervescence that+reads as "polished" rather than "raw citrus." This is a standard trick in luxury fresh fragrances+(MFK Aqua Universalis, Hermes Eau de Citron Noir, Byredo Bal d'Afrique). None of these are+"aldehydic" โ€” they just sparkle.++### Why Oranger Crystals+DHC's grapefruit blossom is beautiful but one-dimensional. Oranger Crystals at 0.012% active adds+a neroli glow BEHIND the blossom โ€” warmth without a second identifiable floral note. Think of this+as backlighting the grapefruit blossom rather than adding a flower. Aurantiol was rejected โ€” too+honeyed, would read as oriental rather than transparent. Neroli EO not in inventory; Oranger Crystals+is the closest neroli-orange-blossom material available and at this dose it contributes texture only.++### Why Damascenone at 0.0005% active+This is the single most class-signaling trace material in perfumery. Damascenone (and its relatives+Beta Damascone, Alpha Damascone, Damascol) create what perfumers call the "rose ketone halo" โ€”+a narcotic floral transparency that makes everything smell more expensive. Used in virtually every+luxury fresh fragrance at doses below 0.001% active. Beta Damascone was considered (slightly+fruitier, more apple-rose) but Damascenone was chosen for its narcotic depth โ€” it reads as+"expensive rose absolute" rather than "fruity floral."++### Why Ambrettolide replaces Ebanol + Coumarin+v2 used Ebanol + Coumarin to reference Allure Homme Edition Blanche's sandalwood-tonka creaminess.+This was a borrowed reference โ€” the formula smelled expensive because it reminded the wearer of+another expensive fragrance. Ambrettolide creates its OWN naturalistic skin warmth. It's the most+luxurious musk in inventory โ€” macrocyclic, fruity-winey, warm without being animalic. At 0.12%+active in concentrate, it creates a "your skin but better" effect that is more classy than+referencing Edition Blanche. Ebanol stays at a reduced dose (0.6% vs 1.4%) as pure texture.++### Why Alpha Irone at 0.005% active+The ultimate Ellena trick. Alpha Irone at the threshold of perception creates an "orris whisper"+that nobody can identify but everybody interprets as "expensive." Used this way in Terre d'Hermes+(iris at trace), Dior Homme (the original โ€” iris as character, not as note), and virtually every+Frederic Malle fresh fragrance. At 10 ยตL of 30% dilution, this is 0.006% active in concentrate โ€”+below the identification threshold for orris (~0.01% is where people start to detect it) but+sufficient to create the "what IS that?" effect.++### Why Hedione HC added+v2 used 950 ยตL of standard Hedione. v3 splits this into 1050 ยตL standard + 100 ยตL HC. HC (high-cis)+has approximately 8ร— the radiance of standard Hedione. The additional 100 ยตL of HC creates superior+jasmonate bloom without increasing volume. This is a premium-but-invisible upgrade โ€” the fragrance+simply radiates better, without the wearer knowing why.++### What was deliberately excluded from v3+- **Coumarin**: removed. The Edition Blanche reference is now internal (Ambrettolide + micro-Ebanol) rather than borrowed.+- **Muguet materials**: same as v2. DHC has no muguet.+- **Additional citruses**: same as v2. One citrus = DHC signature.+- **Additional woods**: same as v2. DHC has no wood character.+- **Scentenal, Calone, Floralozone**: marine/ozone contradict DHC transparency.+- **Galaxolide, Tonalide, Zenolide**: polycyclic musks contradict naturalistic luxury.+- **Habanolide**: warm-skin intimacy is now served by Ambrettolide, which is more naturalistic.+- **Exaltolide**: depleted. Would have been a candidate for additional fatty-skin depth but Ambrettolide covers this register.+- **DBCA, Aurantiol, ACA**: these are white-floral cosmetics that contradict DHC minimalism. Oranger Crystals at micro-dose provides warmth without the cosmetic register.+- **Alpha Damascone, Beta Damascone, Damascol**: the rose-ketone slot is filled by Damascenone at a more narcotic, less fruity register.+- **Benzyl Salicylate, Hexyl Salicylate**: unnecessary fixatives in an 18-material formula. Musk + IES + Ambrofix handle adhesion.++---++## Key OAV Estimates (concentrate)++| Material | Conc in conc (ppm) | Approx ODT | OAV | Perception |+|----------|--------------------|------------|-----|------------|+| Bergamot FCF Sicilian | 220,000 | ~14 ppm | ~15,700 | Massive dominant opening |+| Hedione (total) | 230,000 | ~50 ppm | ~4,600 | Very strong radiance backbone |+| Romandolide | 130,000 | ~2 ppm | ~65,000 | Extremely dominant projection musk |+| Petitgrain EO | 60,000 | ~5 ppm | ~12,000 | Clearly perceptible green-floral bridge |+| Iso E Super | 80,000 | ~0.5 ppm | ~160,000 | Strong skin cocoon |+| Paradisamide (active) | 4,000 | ~0.05 ppb | ~80,000,000 | Extreme impact blossom signature |+| Ambrofix (active) | 9,000 | ~0.3 ppb | ~30,000,000 | Crystalline mineral pillar |+| Ambrettolide (active) | 1,200 | ~0.01 ppm | ~120,000 | Natural skin warmth โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Damascenone (active) | 50 | ~0.02 ppb | ~2,500,000 | Rose-narcotic halo โ€” perceptible despite micro-dose |+| Alpha Irone (active) | 60 | ~0.1 ppb | ~600,000 | Orris whisper โ€” below identification but above ODT |+| Aldehyde C10 (active) | 80 | ~0.5 ppb | ~160,000 | Champagne sparkle โ€” clearly perceptible at opening |+| Oranger Crystals (active) | 1,200 | ~0.1 ppm | ~12,000 | Neroli glow โ€” perceptible warmth |+| Ebanol | 6,000 | ~0.1 ppm | ~60,000 | Sandalwood cream โ€” textural, below note threshold |+| Cardamom EO | 7,000 | ~1 ppm | ~7,000 | Subtle aromatic lift โ€” perceptible but not dominant |+| Linalyl Acetate | 58,000 | ~1 ppm | ~58,000 | Strong citrus-extending freshness |+| Ethyl Linalool | 50,000 | ~0.5 ppm | ~100,000 | Strong woody-floral bridge |+| Hedione HC | 20,000 | ~15 ppm | ~1,333 | Superior radiance โ€” clean jasmonate bloom |+| Ethylene Brassylate | 50,000 | ~1 ppm | ~50,000 | Strong lactonic depth |++*OAVs are in concentrate. After ~6ร— dilution in ethanol, divide all values by 6.*+*All "below identification threshold" materials (Alpha Irone, Aldehyde C10, Oranger Crystals, Damascenone) have OAVs well above 1 โ€” they are perceptible, but below the concentration where the brain identifies them as a distinct note. This is the definition of "classy invisible layer."*++---++## Version History++| Version | Materials | Key difference |+|---------|-----------|----------------|+| v1 | 34 | Overbuilt โ€” muguet complex, 5 woods, 3 citruses. Rejected. |+| v2 | 13 | Correctly minimalist. Clean, transparent. Missing the luxury layer. |+| **v3** | **18** | Classy. Invisible sparkle (Aldehyde C10), rose halo (Damascenone), neroli glow (Oranger Crystals), natural skin warmth (Ambrettolide), orris whisper (Alpha Irone), superior radiance (Hedione HC). Each addition operates below the "note" threshold. |diff --git a/formulas/Transparence_Chanel_Les_Exclusifs_30mL_EdP.md b/formulas/Transparence_Chanel_Les_Exclusifs_30mL_EdP.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..a49699f--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Transparence_Chanel_Les_Exclusifs_30mL_EdP.md@@ -0,0 +1,275 @@+# Transparence โ€” 30 mL Eau de Parfum โ€” Les Exclusifs de Chanel++**Batch:** 30.00 mL ยท ~16.7% EdP ยท **22 materials** (6 EOs/naturals)+**Profile:** Dior Homme Cologne transparency ร— Chanel classical DNA (aldehydes, jasmine-rose-ylang, iris, vetiver, oakmoss)+**Positioning:** Les Exclusifs de Chanel โ€” not Allure Homme, not Bleu de Chanel. Standalone.+A fresh citrus that is to DHC what 1957 is to a simple white musk: the same register, elevated through heritage.+**Maceration:** 4 weeks minimum++---++## Chanel vs Dior: How They Do Transparency Differently++| Axis | Dior (Demachy) | Chanel (Polge) |+|------|---------------|----------------|+| **Philosophy** | 