 Homme+- **Jasmine FO** โ€” Chanel uses real jasmine fractions; Allure Homme uses hedione alone+- **Vetiver + Evernyl** โ€” Chanel's chypre-woody signature (Sycomore, Pour Monsieur); absent from Allure Homme++---++## Equipment++- 1 amber glass bottle 30 mL+- 1 graduated pipette 1 mL (for 15โ€“1050 ยตL)+- 1 micro-pipette or 1 mL syringe graduated 0.01 mL (for 15โ€“50 ยตL)+- Ethanol 96% (perfumer's grade)++---++## Accord Architecture++### Layer 1 โ€” Aldehydic Citrus (Top, ~32% of concentrate)+Chanel's citrus opening is never just citrus โ€” aldehydes are woven in at a dose that reads as+"sparkle" not "aldehydic." Bergamot FCF Sicilian at 21% is the lead (DHC's single citrus).+Cedrat FCF Sicilian at 3.6% adds Chanel's preference for a faceted citrus chord โ€” not two competing+citruses, but bergamot with a mineral edge that reads as "cold glass." Aldehyde C10 + C11 at+1.6% total dilution create the Chanel sparkle โ€” this is the house's fingerprint. Linalyl Acetate+extends bergamot into the heart.++### Layer 2 โ€” The Chanel Floral Whisper (Heart, ~34% of concentrate)+This is where Chanel separates from Dior. DHC is grapefruit blossom alone. Chanel uses grapefruit+blossom (Petitgrain EO, 6%) as the lead floral, but weaves in the classical Chanel trinity at+whisper-level: Jasmine FO at 0.8% (jasmine fractions, not synthetic hedione alone), Damascenone at+0.04% active (the rose whisper โ€” Chanel's rose DNA at the threshold of perception), Ylang Comoros+Complete EO at 0.6% (the ylang whisper โ€” Chanel's No. 5 DNA). Hedione + Hedione HC provide+jasmonate radiance at Chanel volume. Oranger Crystals at 0.3% active adds neroli warmth. Alpha+Irone at 0.009% active is the 1957/La Pausa orris whisper โ€” Chanel cannot make a fragrance without iris.++### Layer 3 โ€” Vetiver-Chypre-Musk Base (Base, ~34% of concentrate)+Romandolide at 13% is the projection white musk โ€” clean, modern. Habanolide at 3% is the Chanel+warm-skin intimacy โ€” 1957 uses a warm musk heavily. Ethylene 