 300 | 300.0 | grapefruit blossom axis โ€” the DHC heart, Chanel-framed |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 150 | 150.0 | high-cis radiance โ€” superior jasmonate bloom |+| 13 | Oranger Crystals | 10% in DPG | 150 | 15.0 | neroli warmth โ€” bridges citrus to the Chanel floral whisper |+| 14 | Jasmine FO | neat | 40 | 40.0 | jasmine whisper โ€” Chanel classical floral trinity: jasmine |+| 15 | Ylang Comoros Complete EO | neat | 30 | 30.0 | ylang whisper โ€” Chanel classical floral trinity: ylang |+| 16 | Damascenone | 1% | 20 | 0.20 | rose whisper โ€” Chanel classical floral trinity: rose |+| 17 | Alpha Irone | 30% in DEP | 15 | 4.5 | orris whisper โ€” 1957 / La Pausa DNA; Chanel cannot make a fragrance without iris |++**Heart subtotal: ~1,705 ยตL** โ€” swirl gently 5 seconds.++---++## Procedure โ€” Layer C: Top (most volatile, last)++| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL | Active ยตL | Role |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|----------:|------|+| 18 | Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 1050 | 1050.0 | lead citrus โ€” the DHC bergamot, framed Chanel |+| 19 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 275 | 275.0 | bergamot companion โ€” extends citrus into Chanel floral |+| 20 | Cedrat FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 180 | 180.0 | mineral-citron edge โ€” Chanel's faceted citrus preference |+| 21 | Aldehyde C10 | 1% | 50 | 0.50 | Chanel fingerprint โ€” citrus sparkle (greener than C11) |+| 22 | Aldehyde C11 | 1% | 30 | 0.30 | Chanel fingerprint โ€” citrus sparkle (more metallic than C10) |++**Top subtotal: ~1,585 ยตL**++2. Concentrate is **~5,050 ยตL**; add approximately **25.0 mL ethanol 96%** (adjust visually to 30 mL line).+   (Excess ~50 ยตL is within acceptable pipetting variance for this batch size.)+3. Cap tightly. Invert **50 times** โ€” gently, no shaking.+4. Label: **"Transparence โ€” Les Exclusifs de Chanel โ€” 2026-05-09 โ€” macerate 4 weeks โ€” open after 2026-06-06"**++---++## Maceration++Store cool and dark. Invert gently once per week.+**Minimum 4 weeks.** This is a Chanel โ€” the aldehydes need time to form Schiff bases with Hedione+and the jasmine-rose-ylang whisper. The vetiver-oakmoss base needs significant integration.+At 2 weeks, the aldehydic citrus has softened. At 3 weeks, the floral whisper begins to cohere.+At 4 weeks, the structure is seamless โ€” the Chanel promise.++---++## Summary Table (all 22 materials)++### Base (9)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 1 | Romandolide | neat | 650 |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 400 |+| 3 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 250 |+| 4 | Habanolide | neat | 150 |+| 5 | Ambrofix | 30% | 120 |+| 6 | Clearwood | neat | 80 |+| 7 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 50 |+| 8 | Vetiver EO India | neat | 40 |+| 9 | Evernyl | neat | 20 |++### Heart (8)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 10 | Hedione | neat | 1000 |+| 11 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 300 |+| 12 | Hedione HC | neat | 150 |+| 13 | Oranger Crystals | 10% in DPG | 150 |+| 14 | Jasmine FO | neat | 40 |+| 15 | Ylang Comoros Complete EO | neat | 30 |+| 16 | Damascenone | 1% | 20 |+| 17 | Alpha Irone | 30% in DEP | 15 |++### Top (5)+| # | Material | Dilution | ยตL |+|--:|----------|----------|----:|+| 18 | Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 1050 |+| 19 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 275 |+| 20 | Cedrat FCF oil Sicilian | neat | 180 |+| 21 | Aldehyde C10 | 1% | 50 |+| 22 | Aldehyde C11 | 1% | 30 |++---++## Chanel DNA โ€” Material Justifications++### Why aldehydes C10 + C11 (and not just one)+Chanel is the house of aldehydes. No. 5, No. 22, No. 5 L'EAU, 1957 all use aldehyde chords,+not single aldehydes. C10 provides green-citrus sparkle. C11 provides metallic-citrus sparkle.+Together they create the Chanel "champagne" opening that a single aldehyde cannot. At 0.001%+and 0.0006% active respectively, they operate well below the classical "aldehydic" threshold+(No. 5 uses aldehydes at 10-100ร— these doses). This is 1957 / No. 5 L'EAU proportion โ€” present+but transparent.++### Why Jasmine FO + Damascenone + Ylang (the Chanel trinity)+Every Chanel fragrance, however transparent, carries the house's classical floral DNA: jasmine,+rose, ylang. No. 5, No. 5 L'EAU, 1957, Coco, Coco Mademoiselle, even Bleu de Chanel has a+jasmine undertone. Jasmine FO at 0.8% is the jasmine whisper โ€” not enough to register as "jasmine,"+enough to register as "Chanel." Damascenone at 0.0004% active is the rose whisper โ€” below+identification. Ylang at 0.6% is the ylang whisper โ€” detectable only as warmth. Together they+create the Chanel floral hum.++### Why Habanolide+Chanel's musks are warmer and more intimate than Dior's. 1957 is built around a warm white musk.+Habanolide's warm-skin intimacy is the correct Chanel register. It sits ON skin and makes the+wearer smell clean and warm simultaneously. Romandolide handles projection; Habanolide handles+intimacy. This is Chanel's musk philosophy โ€” layered, not singular.++### Why Vetiver + Evernyl (the Chanel woody-chypre signature)+Chanel never fully abandons classical French perfumery structure. Sycomore is a vetiver soliflore.+Pour Monsieur is an oakmoss chypre. Even Bleu de Chanel has an oakmoss-vetiver backbone.+Vetiver EO India at 0.8% is a whisper of Sycomore โ€” the earthy-woody texture that prevents the+base from becoming purely cosmetic. Evernyl at 0.4% is the oakmoss whisper โ€” a trace of chypre+sophistication that adds longevity and class.++### Why Oranger Crystals over Aurantiol+Aurantiol is honeyed โ€” too warm, too sweet for a transparent Chanel. Oranger Crystals at 0.3%+active adds neroli character without honeyed sweetness or oriental weight. It bridges the+aldehydic citrus opening to the jasmine-rose-ylang whisper.++### Why no Paradisamide+DHC uses a paradisi-type material for its grapefruit blossom. Chanel would not โ€” the tropical-+guava character of Paradisamide reads as "niche-synthetic" rather than "classical Chanel."+Chanel achieves grapefruit blossom through Petitgrain EO (the classical material) supported+by aldehydes (for sparkle) and jasmine (for warmth). The result is more blended, less distinctly+"tropical."++### What was rejected and why+- **Lavender, geranium, clary sage, rosemary**: Allure Homme / fougere territory. Not Les Exclusifs.+- **Coumarin**: Allure Homme Edition Blanche signature. Deliberately absent to maintain separation.+- **Dihydromyrcenol**: Allure Homme Sport / Bleu de Chanel laundry-freshness. Too mass-market.+- **Calone, Floralozone, Scentenal**: Aquatic-ozone direction belongs to Allure Homme Sport, not Les Exclusifs.+- **Cashmeran, Azarbre**: Textile-warmth and warm-amber register. These are modern niche materials Chanel uses sparingly. For Transparence, the warmth comes from Chanel's classical sources (jasmine, ylang, musk), not from modern woody-ambers.+- **Galaxolide, Tonalide**: Polycyclic laundry musks. Chanel's Les Exclusifs line uses macrocyclic and naturalistic musks.+- **Black Pepper, Pink Pepper, Juniper**: Spicy-aromatic lift belongs to Bleu de Chanel and Allure Homme Sport. Aldehydes provide the lift instead.+- **Patchouli**: Too earthy-heavy for this transparent concept. Clearwood provides wood without earth.+- **Benzyl Salicylate, Hexyl Salicylate**: Cosmetic fixatives. Chanel's musk chord + vetiver + evernyl provide sufficient fixation.+- **DBCA, ACA, Aurantiol**: White-floral cosmetics that would make this read as "floral perfume" rather than "transparent citrus."+- **Heliotropin / Heliotropal**: Powdery-almond sweetness belongs to Chanel's oriental compositions (Coromandel), not a transparent citrus.+- **Methyl Pamplemousse, Paradisamide**: Synthetic grapefruit modifiers. Chanel achieves the grapefruit register through Petitgrain + aldehydes. The synthetic fruit direction reads as "modern niche" not "classical Chanel."+- **Citronellol, Geraniol, PEA**: Individual rose materials. Damascenone at micro-dose provides the rose whisper more elegantly than a blend of rose chemicals.+- **Beta Ionone, Alpha Ionone**: Additional ionones. Alpha Irone alone at micro-dose is more Chanel โ€” the house prefers irone to ionone for the orris register.++---++## Key OAV Estimates (concentrate)++| Material | Conc in conc (ppm) | Approx ODT | OAV | Perception |+|----------|--------------------|------------|-----|------------|+| Bergamot FCF Sicilian | 210,000 | ~14 ppm | ~15,000 | Massive dominant opening |+| Hedione (total) | 230,000 | ~50 ppm | ~4,600 | Very strong radiance |+| Romandolide | 130,000 | ~2 ppm | ~65,000 | Extremely dominant projection musk |+| Petitgrain EO | 60,000 | ~5 ppm | ~12,000 | Clearly perceptible grapefruit blossom |+| Iso E Super | 80,000 | ~0.5 ppm | ~160,000 | Strong skin cocoon |+| Habanolide | 30,000 | ~1 ppm | ~30,000 | Warm skin intimacy โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Ethylene Brassylate | 50,000 | ~1 ppm | ~50,000 | Strong lactonic depth |+| Ambrofix (active) | 7,200 | ~0.3 ppb | ~24,000,000 | Crystalline pillar |+| Ylang EO | 6,000 | ~0.1 ppm | ~60,000 | Ylang warmth โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Jasmine FO | 8,000 | ~1 ppm* | ~8,000 | Jasmine whisper โ€” perceptible as "floral warmth" |+| Damascenone (active) | 40 | ~0.02 ppb | ~2,000,000 | Rose-narcotic halo โ€” perceptible despite micro-dose |+| Alpha Irone (active) | 90 | ~0.1 ppb | ~900,000 | Orris whisper โ€” below identification, above ODT |+| Aldehyde C10 (active) | 100 | ~0.5 ppb | ~200,000 | Chanel sparkle โ€” clearly perceptible at opening |+| Aldehyde C11 (active) | 60 | ~0.3 ppb | ~200,000 | Chanel sparkle โ€” more metallic than C10 |+| Oranger Crystals (active) | 3,000 | ~0.1 ppm | ~30,000 | Neroli warmth โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Ambrettolide (active) | 1,000 | ~0.01 ppm | ~100,000 | Natural skin warmth โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Vetiver EO India | 8,000 | ~0.5 ppm | ~16,000 | Earthy-woody โ€” clearly perceptible as texture |+| Evernyl | 4,000 | ~0.05 ppm | ~80,000 | Oakmoss whisper โ€” strong chypre anchor |+| Cedrat FCF Sicilian | 36,000 | ~5 ppm | ~7,200 | Mineral-citron edge โ€” clearly perceptible |+| Linalyl Acetate | 55,000 | ~1 ppm | ~55,000 | Citrus-extending freshness |+| Clearwood | 16,000 | ~1 ppm | ~16,000 | Clean woody structure |++*OAVs are in concentrate. After ~6ร— dilution in ethanol, divide all values by 6.*+*Jasmine FO threshold estimated based on typical jasmine absolute ODT in ethanol.*diff --git a/formulas/Tropicale_Gourmande_10mL_EDP.md b/formulas/Tropicale_Gourmande_10mL_EDP.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..14d1066--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Tropicale_Gourmande_10mL_EDP.md@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@+# Tropicale Gourmande โ€” 10 mL EDP++**Fragrance Family:** Fruity Gourmand (Gourmand subfamily โ€” tropical fruit character)+**Concentrate:** 16.0% (1,600 ยตL in 10.00 mL)+**Version:** v2 โ€” Heliotropal swap + IFRA compliance++---++## Formula++| # | Ingredient | Dilution | Amount (ยตL) | Amount (mL) |+|---|-----------|----------|-------------|-------------|+| **TOP โ€” Pineapple-Coconut Opening** |+| 1 | Allyl Amyl Glycolate | neat | 60 | 0.060 |+| 2 | Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate | neat | 40 | 0.040 |+| 3 | Paradisamide | 10% | 80 | 0.080 |+| 4 | Aldehyde C10 | 1% | 60 | 0.060 |+| **HEART โ€” Tropical Floral + Coconut Cream Bridge** |+| 5 | Gamma Decalactone | neat | 50 | 0.050 |+| 6 | Gamma Undecalactone | neat | 70 | 0.070 |+| 7 | Delta Decalactone | neat | 40 | 0.040 |+| 8 | Maple Lactone | 20% | 40 | 0.040 |+| 9 | Ylang Ylang EO (Extra) | neat | 80 | 0.080 |+| 10 | Hedione | neat | 240 | 0.240 |+| **BASE โ€” Vanilla Gourmand Bed** |+| 11 | Vanillin | 10% | 240 | 0.240 |+| 12 | Ethyl Vanillin | neat | 40 | 0.040 |+| 13 | Coumarin | 20% | 70 | 0.070 |+| 14 | Siam Benzoin | 50% in DPG | 80 | 0.080 |+| 15 | Heliotropal (Piperonal) | neat | 30 | 0.030 |+| 16 | Benzyl Salicylate | neat | 80 | 0.080 |+| 17 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 100 | 0.100 |+| 18 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 60 | 0.060 |+| 19 | Romandolide | neat | 60 | 0.060 |+| 20 | Iso E Super | neat | 80 | 0.080 |+| **DILUTION** |+| 21 | Ethanol 96% | โ€” | โ€” | 8.40 |++**Total concentrate:** 1.60 mL | **Total volume:** 10.00 mL | **Concentrate:** 16.0%++---++## Musk Chord++| Axis | Material | Amount |+|------|----------|--------|+| Depth | Ethylene Brassylate (neat) | 100 ยตL |+| Projection | Romandolide (neat) | 60 ยตL |+| Character-Echo | Ambrettolide (10% in DPG) | 60 ยตL |diff --git a/formulas/Tropicale_Gourmande_30mL_EDP.md b/formulas/Tropicale_Gourmande_30mL_EDP.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..ae2af45--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/Tropicale_Gourmande_30mL_EDP.md@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@+# Tropicale Gourmande โ€” 30 mL EDP++**Fragrance Family:** Fruity Gourmand (Gourmand subfamily โ€” tropical fruit character)+**Concentrate:** 16.0% (4,800 ยตL in 30.00 mL)+**Version:** v2 โ€” Heliotropal swap + IFRA compliance++---++## Formula++| # | Ingredient | Dilution | Amount (ยตL) | Amount (mL) |+|---|-----------|----------|-------------|-------------|+| **TOP โ€” Pineapple-Coconut Opening** |+| 1 | Allyl Amyl Glycolate | neat | 180 | 0.180 |+| 2 | Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate | neat | 120 | 0.120 |+| 3 | Paradisamide | 10% | 240 | 0.240 |+| 4 | Aldehyde C10 | 1% | 180 | 0.180 |+| **HEART โ€” Tropical Floral + Coconut Cream Bridge** |+| 5 | Gamma Decalactone | neat | 150 | 0.150 |+| 6 | Gamma Undecalactone | neat | 210 | 0.210 |+| 7 | Delta Decalactone | neat | 120 | 0.120 |+| 8 | Maple Lactone | 20% | 120 | 0.120 |+| 9 | Ylang Ylang EO (Extra) | neat | 240 | 0.240 |+| 10 | Hedione | neat | 720 | 0.720 |+| **BASE โ€” Vanilla Gourmand Bed** |+| 11 | Vanillin | 10% | 720 | 0.720 |+| 12 | Ethyl Vanillin | neat | 120 | 0.120 |+| 13 | Coumarin | 20% | 210 | 0.210 |+| 14 | Siam Benzoin | 50% in DPG | 240 | 0.240 |+| 15 | Heliotropal (Piperonal) | neat | 90 | 0.090 |+| 16 | Benzyl Salicylate | neat | 240 | 0.240 |+| 17 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 300 | 0.300 |+| 18 | Ambrettolide | 10% in DPG | 180 | 0.180 |+| 19 | Romandolide | neat | 180 | 0.180 |+| 20 | Iso E Super | neat | 240 | 0.240 |+| **DILUTION** |+| 21 | Ethanol 96% | โ€” | โ€” | 25.20 |++**Total concentrate:** 4.80 mL | **Total v