nsparent jasmine-muguet radiance (Hedione HC + Hedione + Mayol + Hydroxycitronellal) and reinvests the material budget into a stronger, more persistent green character that carries from opening through drydown.++> **What changed vs F2:**+> - **Stronger green throughout:** Galbanum + Dynascone + Hexenol in the top; Verdox + Cyclamen Aldehyde + Parmavert in the heart extend green persistence beyond the first 20 minutes.+> - **Leaner floral heart:** No ACA, Benzyl Acetate, Ylang, PCME, Damascone, Damascol, Cis Jasmone, Geraniol, or Bourgeonal. The heart is transparent jasmine-muguet on Iz E Super velvet โ€” the Cristalle trick โ€” not a lush floral bouquet.+> - **Warmer amber base:** Ambermax + Azarbre replace Ambrofix. Green chypre reads best with warm rounded amber (the "moss on warm stone" effect), not cold crystalline amber.+> - **Coumarin in chypre dose:** 40 ยตL active โ€” warm without crossing into fougรจre territory.+> - **No animalic shock materials:** No IBQ, Birch Tar, Indole, Skatole. Polished drydown for mass market.++> **The three structural chords:**+> 1. **Green Chypre Axis:** Galbanum โ’ Hexenol โ’ Dynascone โ’ Verdox โ’ Cyclamen Aldehyde โ’ Evernyl โ’ Patchouli โ’ Vetiver โ’ Cedarwood Virginia. Green character persists through all three pyramid stages, not just the top.+> 2. **Jasmonate Radiance + Muguet Transparency:** Hedione HC + Hedione (mustard/wine full-spectrum jasmonate; not defaulting โ€” HC specifically for its depth dimension), with Mayol + Hydroxycitronellal as transparent muguet (the No. 19/Cristalle heart strategy).+> 3. **3-Axis Musk + Texture Cushion:** Galaxolide (projection axis) + Ethylene Brassylate (depth axis) + Ambrettolide (character-echo axis โ€” warm-green naturalistic skin), with Iso E Super as molecular velvet and Cashmeran as textile warmth in the drydown.++---++## What you'll need++- 1 ร— clean 30 mL atomizer or amber bottle (final bottle)+- 1 ร— clean 10 mL amber vial (concentrate build vial)+- Positive-displacement pipette 10โ€“100 ยตL (trace doses)+- Standard pipette 100โ€“1000 ยตL+- 1 mL glass syringe or graduated dropper for larger volumes+- Perfumer's ethanol โฅ 96 %, fragrance-grade++> Build the **6 mL concentrate first**, mature 4+ weeks, then dilute. Galbanum + Dynascone + Evernyl + macrocyclic musks all need maturation to shed their "ingredient-list" reading.++---++## Architecture++| Layer | Function | Key materials |+|---|---|---|+| **Top** | Sparkling green-citrus opening with galbanum stem-sap | Bergamot FCF Sicilian, Cedrat FCF Sicilian, Petitgrain, Galbanum Resinoid, cis-3-Hexenol, Dynascone, Triplal, Dihydromyrcenol, Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate, Aldehyde C12 MNA |+| **Heart** | Transparent jasmonate-muguet radiance on Iso E Super velvet; green persistence bridging into base | Hedione HC, Hedione, Iso E Super, Hydroxycitronellal, Cyclamen Aldehyde, Mayol, Verdox, Parmavert, PEA |+| **Base** | Chypre spine (patchouli-vetiver-evernyl-cedarwood) + warm amber cushion + 3-axis musk chord | Patchouli, Galaxolide, Vetiver, Ethylene Brassylate, Cedarwood Virginia, Evernyl, Ambermax, Coumarin, Azarbre, Ambrettolide, Benzoin Resinoid, Cashmeran, Ebanol, Hexyl Salicylate, Benzyl Benzoate |++---++## Step 1 โ€” Build the 6 mL concentrate++> All additions go into the **10 mL amber build vial**. Cap and swirl gently after each addition. Use a fresh pipette tip per material.++### Stage 1A โ€” Base (15 materials, 3 353 ยตL)++| # | Material | Form | ยตL | mL |+|---:|---|---|---:|---:|+| 20 | Patchouli EO | neat | 540 | 0.540 |+| 21 | Galaxolide | 80 % | 400 | 0.400 |+| 22 | Vetiver EO | neat | 340 | 0.340 |+| 23 | Ethylene Brassylate | neat | 313 | 0.313 |+| 24 | Cedarwood oil Virginia | neat | 280 | 0.280 |+| 25 | Evernyl | neat | 260 | 0.260 |+| 26 | Ambermax | 50 % | 260 | 0.260 |+| 27 | Coumarin | 20 % in DPG | 200 | 0.200 |+| 28 | Azarbre | neat | 150 | 0.150 |+| 29 | Ambrettolide | 10 % in DPG | 180 | 0.180 |+| 30 | Benzoin Resinoid | 50 % in DPG | 150 | 0.150 |+| 31 | Cashme