efore adding more volatile materials on top.++---++## OAV / Scoring follow-up++Per the open scheduling offer from the prior turn โ€” schedule an agent (in 1 week, after a brief soak) to:+1. Run all 18 v3 baseline + differentiation-augmented formulas through `engine/optimizer/oav_guard.py` `check_proportional_scaling()`.+2. Run all 36 builds (18 base + 18 augmented) through `engine/optimizer/scoring.py` FormulaScorer on the 10 axes.+3. Compare ฮ”Luxury, ฮ”Longevity, ฮ”Performance, ฮ”Depth, ฮ”Texture between baseline and augmented per build.+4. Flag any addition that fails to materially improve its target axis (โฅ 5 % lift) โ€” those become candidates for re-tuning.++This needs the formulas in structured (JSON / Python dict) form for the scoring engine to ingest. Recommend: write a one-time parser at `scripts/parse_collection_md_to_json.py` that reads the markdown formula tables and emits a JSON file the FormulaScorer can ingest. That's the prerequisite step before the scoring agent can run.diff --git a/formulas/collections/F1_Le_Barbier_de_Grasse_30mL_EDP_Optimized.md b/formulas/collections/F1_Le_Barbier_de_Grasse_30mL_EDP_Optimized.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..6c8edfc--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/collections/F1_Le_Barbier_de_Grasse_30mL_EDP_Optimized.md@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@+# F1 โ€” Le Barbier de Grasse โ€” Optimized 30 mL EDP++*Classical fougere โ€” bergamot, lavender, coumarin, mossy cedar, amber-musk restraint.*++**Status:** OAV differential-evolution optimized (DE/rand/1/bin, 50 generations).+**Score delta vs initial:** +1435425.225++---++## Concept Brief++A classical French barbershop fougere built around a lavender-coumarin axis, with bergamot lift, mossy cedar shadow, and a soft amber-musk bed. The brief is not modern sweet mass-appeal and not dense gourmand amber. Keep the structure recognisably fougere: aromatic top and heart must stay legible, coumarin must remain the warm hay signature, Evernyl must read as moss-shadow rather than bitterness, and the amber-musks should support rather than dominate. Vanilla warmth is welcome only as polish. Preserve elegance, dryness, and grooming-soap clarity over syrup or loud projection.++---++## Batch Parameters++| Parameter | Value |+|---|---|+| Total batch | 30 mL |+| EDP concentration | 20% |+| Fragrance concentrate | 6.0 mL (6000 ยตL) |+| Ethanol 96% (dilution) | 24.0 mL (24000 ยตL) |++## Optimized Formula โ€” 30 mL EDP++| # | Material | wt% | ยตL | mL | ~Drops |+|--:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|+| 1 | Coumarin | 21.15 | 1269 | 1.269 | 63.5 |+| 2 | Hedione | 13.18 | 791 | 0.791 | 39.5 |+| 3 | Iso E Super | 10.67 | 640 | 0.640 | 32.0 |+| 4 | Ethylene Brassylate | 7.14 | 428 | 0.428 | 21.4 |+| 5 | Galaxolide | 6.32 | 379 | 0.379 | 19.0 |+| 6 | Lavender EO | 6.20 | 372 | 0.372 | 18.6 |+| 7 | Ambrox Super | 6.13 | 368 | 0.368 | 18.4 |+| 8 | Cedarwood EO | 5.50 | 330 | 0.330 | 16.5 |+| 9 | Vanillin | 4.46 | 268 | 0.268 | 13.4 |+| 10 | Patchouli EO | 4.07 | 244 | 0.244 | 12.2 |+| 11 | Linalyl Acetate | 3.56 | 214 | 0.214 | 10.7 |+| 12 | Vetiver EO | 2.69 | 161 | 0.161 | 8.1 |+| 13 | Geraniol | 2.64 | 158 | 0.158 | 7.9 |+| 14 | Bergamot FCF | 2.03 | 122 | 0.122 | 6.1 |+| 15 | Evernyl | 1.74 | 105 | 0.105 | 5.2 |+| 16 | Hexyl Salicylate | 1.44 | 87 | 0.087 | 4.3 |+| 17 | Eugenol | 1.08 | 65 | 0.065 | 3.2 |+| โ€” | **Fragrance sub-total** | **100.00** | **6000** | **6.000** | โ€” |+| โ€” | Ethanol 96% (in concentrate) | โ€” | 0 | 0.000 | โ€” |+| โ€” | **Concentrate total** | โ€” | **6000** | **6.000** | โ€” |+| โ€” | Ethanol 96% (bottle fill) | โ€” | **24000** | **24.000** | โ€” |+| โ€” | **Final bottle total** | โ€” | **30000** | **30.000** | โ€” |++## wt% Comparison (Initial โ’ Optimized)++| Material | Initial | Optimized | ฮ” |+|---|---:|---:|---:|+| Coumarin | 19.47 | 21.15 | +1.69 |+| Hedione | 12.37 | 13.18 | +0.81 |+| Iso E Super | 9.95 | 10.67 | +0.72 |+| Ethylene Brassylate | 6.62 | 7.14 | +0.52 |+| Galaxolide | 6.43 | 6.32 | -0.11 |+| Lavender EO | 5.92 | 6.20 | +0.29 |+| Amb