r | Vol d'Ambre v4 |+|---|---|---|+| Opening | Bergamot + lavender (aromatic leads) | Bergamot + apple (fruity leads) |+| Heart | Hedione + coumarin sweetness | Hedione HC + amber warmth building |+| Drydown | Coumarin + oakmoss (Evernyl) + dry vetiver/cedar | Ambrox + vanilla + creamy Sandalore |+| Amber OAV (base) | ~40 | ~321 |+| Aromatic OAV (base) | ~383 | ~149 |+| Character | Diffuse, dry, barbershop | Skin-close, warm, opulent |+| Family position | Classic/heritage fougรจre | Modern fougรจre-oriental |++Evernyl is the key ingredient to smell. It smells like wet stone, moss, damp forest floor โ€” nothing else in your inventory does this. It is what gives the classical fougรจre its distinctive bitter-green shadow that Layton does not have.++---++## Safety Notes++- **Evernyl:** oakmoss-type allergen. IFRA Cat 4 limit 0.02 % in finished product. At 2.31 % of concentrate in 20 % EDP โ’ 0.46 % in EDP โ€” **exceeds IFRA limit for leave-on skin use.** For evaluation/testing purposes this is acceptable; do not wear daily. Evernyl's limit is 0.1 % neat in EDP (= 0.5 % in concentrate at 20 % EDP) โ€” just on the edge. If reducing, cut to 70 ยตL (1 %) in concentrate.+- **Eugenol:** IFRA Cat 4 limit ~1.0 % in finished product. At 1.48 % of concentrate ร— 20 % = 0.30 % in EDP. Safe.+- **Bergamot FCF:** FCF = furanocoumarin-free, no phototoxicity risk.+- **Coumarin:** IFRA Cat 4 limit 3.5 % of concentrate. At 5.32 % in concentrate โ€” **slightly over IFRA limit.** Reduce to 210 ยตL (= 3.5 % of 6000 ยตL) if IFRA compliance is required. For evaluation/testing batches the current level is acceptable.diff --git a/formulas/collections/Mass_Market_Masculine_Fougere_3_Variations.md b/formulas/collections/Mass_Market_Masculine_Fougere_3_Variations.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..c031534--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/collections/Mass_Market_Masculine_Fougere_3_Variations.md@@ -0,0 +1,308 @@+# Mass-Market Masculine Aromatic Fougรจre โ€” Education Set, 3 Variations++**Date:** 2026-04-30+**Goal:** train the discipline of *subtraction* by building three clean mass-market masculine aromatic fougรจres from zero. Each is a 30 mL EDP at 20% concentration. Each is built around a different archetype spanning 33 years of the category.++---++## The Educational Decision++**Choice: educate on mass-market masculine aromatic fougรจre, not a different family.**++Reasoning:++1. **The real gap.** The `Vol d'Ambre v3c` exercise just exposed an honest weakness โ€” the user's formulation reflex is amber-fruity-floral-gourmand maximalism. Every bottle includes vanilla + benzoin + multiple jasmines + roses + apple + cardamom + amber. This is one mode. Mass-market masculine fougรจre is the *opposite mode*: cold, dry, restrained, deliberately incomplete. **Learning to omit is harder than learning to add.**+2. **Direct commercial relevance.** Sauvage / Bleu de Chanel / Acqua di Giรฒ Profondo dominate Thai mass-market masculine. The user already lives in this market. Building one clean version of each archetype teaches the category from the inside.+3. **No new materials needed.** The existing inventory already contains every material required. A different family (chypre, floral aldehydic, leather) would require new purchases and slow the loop.+4. **Best ROI per learning hour.** The user already has the perfumery vocabulary; what they lack is restraint. This is a discipline problem, not a knowledge problem. The quickest fix is forced practice.++**What this set is *not*:** dupe-cloning. These are *archetype-correct* compositions in the spirit of Sauvage / Bleu / Drakkar, not 1:1 clones. The point is the architecture, not the smell-alike.++---++## Common Architecture++All three follow the same five-tier mass-market masculine aromatic fougรจre skeleton:++| Tier | Function | Materials by category |+|---|---|---|+| Citrus top | volatile <5 min, first impression | bergamot, grapefruit, lime, citron, petitgrain |+| Aromatic heart | 5โ€“60 min, family-defining axis | lavender, linalyl acetate, clary sage, geraniol, juniper |+| Spice/pepper hook | bite, modernity | cardamom, eugenol; in V3 omitted |+| Coumarin/tonka | sweetness *bridge*, not gourmand load | coumarin only; no vanilla, no benzoin |+| Woody/musky/amber base | longevity and projection | Iso E Super, cedarwood, sandalore, Ambrox, musks |++**Forbidden in this set:**++- Vanillin, Ethyl Vanillin, Benzoin Resinoid (gourmand load โ€” disqualifies the family read).+- Apritone, Hexyl Acetate, Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate (apple esters โ€” push toward fruity-amber).+- Hedione HC (out of stock anyway).+- Multiple jasmines or roses (kitchen-sink floral mass).+- Cashmeran above trace (creamy-warm pulls toward oriental).+- Norlimbanol Dextro above 0.3% concentrate (woody OR overload risk in clean fougรจre).++This list is the *learning point*. None of these are bad materials โ€” they are simply category-disqualifying for clean masculine fougรจre.++---++## V1 โ€” Cold Pepper Fougรจre (Sauvage EDP Archetype, 2015+)++**Character target:** cold, metallic, peppery; dry citrus over cardamom-eugenol "pepper" effect; aromatic lavender heart; massive Ambrox skin warmth; Iso E Super transparent woody trail. Should read as the Sauvage tier โ€” masculine, projection-forward, slightly synthetic-clean.++**Concentration target:** Ambrox `2.00%` neat EDP (Sauvage EDP parity). Total concentrate `~30%` of bottle = strong EDP / weak parfum tier.++### Concentrate (6,000 ยตL โ’ 20% in 30 mL)++| # | Material | Stock | ยตL | wt% conc | Tier |+| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |+| 1 | Ambrox Super | 30% | 1,960 | 32.67 | base |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 720 | 12.00 | base |+| 3 | Bergamot FCF | neat | 600 | 10.00 | top |+| 4 | Hedione | neat | 360 | 6.00 | heart |+| 5 | Lavender EO | neat | 360 | 6.00 | heart |+| 6 | Cedarwood Virginia | neat | 300 | 5.00 | base |+| 7 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 240 | 4.00 | heart |+| 8 | Cardamom FTEC | 10% | 240 | 4.00 | top/heart |+| 9 | Habanolide | neat | 240 | 4.00 | base |+| 10 | Galaxolide | neat | 180 | 3.00 | base |+| 11 | Lime Distilled EO | neat | 150 | 2.50 | top |+| 12 | Geraniol | neat | 120 | 2.00 | heart |+| 13 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 120 | 2.00 | top |+| 14 | Coumarin | 20% | 90 | 1.50 | base |+| 15 | Clary Sage EO | neat | 90 | 1.50 | heart |+| 16 | Eugenol | neat | 60 | 1.00 | heart |+| 17 | Timberol | neat | 60 | 1.00 | base |+| 18 | Cashmeran | neat | 60 | 1.00 | base (trace) |+| 19 | Beta-Pinene | neat | 30 | 0.50 | top |+| 20 | Norlimbanol Dextro | neat | 18 | 0.30 | base (trace) |+| โ€” | BHT | neat | 1.2 | 0.02 | antioxidant |+| โ€” | **Total concentrate** | โ€” | **~6,000** | **100.00** | โ€” |+| โ€” | Ethanol 96% (bottle fill) | โ€” | 24,000 | โ€” | carrier |+| โ€” | **Final bottle total** | โ€” | **30,000** | โ€” | โ€” |++**Neat-equivalent in EDP** (key materials):++| Material | wt% in 30 mL EDP (neat) |+| --- | ---: |+| Ambrox Super (active) | 1.96% |+| Iso E Super | 2.40% |+| Bergamot FCF | 2.00% |+| Lavender EO | 1.20% |+| Linalyl Acetate | 0.80% |+| Eugenol | 0.20% |+| Coumarin (active) | 0.06% |+| Evernyl | 0% (intentionally absent) |++### Why This Reads Like Sauvage++- **Ambrox at `1.96%` neat** โ€” Sauvage EDP parity. This is the dominant character marker.+- **No Evernyl.** Modern Sauvage-tier does not use moss; the family read comes from lavender + coumarin + Iso E Super + dry cedar woody framework.+- **Cardamom FTEC + Eugenol = "pink pepper proxy."** No real pink pepper EO needed; the eugenol-clove + cardamom-ginger combination delivers the same OR signal at the heart-aromatic boundary.+- **Heavy Iso E Super (`2.40%` neat)** โ€” gives the transparent-woody Sauvage signature without competing with the aromatic heart.+- **Habanolide + Galaxolide = `1.40%` musks** โ€” clean white-musk trail for skin-projection, no animalic.+- **Beta-Pinene `0.50%`** โ€” pine-resin sparkle in the top, a defining Sauvage facet.+- **Lavender at `1.20%` neat, no spike lavender** โ€” Sauvage uses smooth lavender, not the camphoraceous spike profile.++### What V1 Teaches++The discipline of building a high-Ambrox modern fougรจre with **only the materials the family needs**. No vanilla, no benzoin, no fruit, no rose, no jasmine body. The lavender + Hedione is the *only* heart bridge.++---++## V2 โ€” Cedar-Iso E Modern Fougรจre (Bleu de Chanel EDP Archetype, 2010+)++**Character target:** cleaner and more transparent than V1; grapefruit-led citrus over Iso E Super dominant body; cedar-sandalwood base; slightly less Ambrox; trace ginger-pepper; refined and approachable rather than aggressive. Should read as the Bleu de Chanel tier โ€” modern, polished, easy to wear.++**Concentration target:** Ambrox `1.50%` neat EDP (Bleu de Chanel-tier). Iso E Super dominant at `4.00%` neat (signature mass).++### Concentrate (6,000 ยตL โ’ 20% in 30 mL)++| # | Material | Stock | ยตL | wt% conc | Tier |+| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |+| 1 | Ambrox Super | 30% | 1,500 | 25.00 | base |+| 2 | Iso E Super | neat | 1,200 | 20.00 | base/heart |+| 3 | Grapefruit FCF | neat | 480 | 8.00 | top |+| 4 | Hedione | neat | 480 | 8.00 | heart |+| 5 | Cedarwood Virginia | neat | 360 | 6.00 | base |+| 6 | Sandalore | neat | 300 | 5.00 | base |+| 7 | Bergamot FCF | neat | 300 | 5.00 | top |+| 8 | Lavender EO | neat | 240 | 4.00 | heart |+| 9 | Habanolide | neat | 240 | 4.00 | base |+| 10 | Linalyl Acetate | neat | 180 | 3.00 | heart |+| 11 | Galaxolide | neat | 180 | 3.00 | base |+| 12 | Coumarin | 20% | 90 | 1.50 | base |+| 13 | Cashmeran | neat | 90 | 1.50 | base |+| 14 | Petitgrain EO | neat | 90 | 1.50 | top |+| 15 | Cardamom FTEC | 10% | 60 | 1.00 | top/heart |+| 16 | Lime Distilled EO | neat | 60 | 1.00 | top |+| 17 | Phenethyl Alcohol | neat | 60 | 1.00 | heart |+| 18 | Geraniol | neat | 30 | 0.50 | heart |+| 19 | Beta-Pinene | neat | 30 | 0.50 | top |+| 20 | Vetiver EO | neat | 30 | 0.50 | base (trace) |+| โ€” | BHT | neat | 1.2 | 0.02 | antioxidant |+| โ€” | **Total concentrate** | โ€” | **~6,000** | **100.00** | โ€” |+| โ€” | Ethanol 96% (bottle fill) | โ€” | 24,000 | โ€” | carrier |+| โ€” | **Final bottle total** | โ€” | **30,000** | โ€” | โ€” |++**Neat-equivalent in EDP** (key materials):++| Material | wt% in 30 mL EDP (neat) |+| --- | ---: |+| Ambrox Super (active) | 1.50% |+| Iso E Super | 4.00% |+| Grapefruit FCF | 1.60% |+| Bergamot FCF | 1.00% |+| Hedione | 1.60% |+| Cedarwood Virginia | 1.20% |+| Sandalore | 1.00% |+| Lavender EO | 0.80% |+| Vetiver EO | 0.10% |++### Why This Reads Like Bleu de Chanel++- **Iso E Super at `4.00%` neat** โ€” the highest concentration in this set. Bleu de Chanel is structurally an Iso E Super perfume; everything else is in service of it. This is the architectural choice.+- **Lower Ambrox (`1.50%` neat)** โ€” present but not dominant; the cedar-sandalwood-Iso E carry the projection instead.+- **Grapefruit FCF + Bergamot + Lime + Petitgrain** โ€” modern bright citrus block, slightly bitter. No sweetness in the top.+- **Cedar Virginia + Sandalore + trace Vetiver** โ€” woody base with sandalwood softness, not the dry-cedar-only profile of V1.+- **Phenethyl Alcohol `1.0%`** โ€” small rose-water note that softens the masculine edge without becoming feminine. This is one of Bleu de Chanel's quiet signatures.+- **Cashmeran `1.50%` (allowed here, unlike V1's trace)** โ€” modern creamy woody character.+- **Lavender quieter (`0.80%` neat)** โ€” Bleu de Chanel uses lavender as a supporting note, not a lead. The aromatic heart is more about Hedione + Iso E than lavender.++### What V2 Teaches++How to build a fougรจre around **a single dominant material (Iso E Super) instead of around lavender**. This is the signature trick of modern designer masculine fougรจre โ€” pick one big diffusion material as the architecture and let everything else decorate it.++---++## V3 โ€” Classic Aromatic Fougรจre (Drakkar Noir 1982 Archetype)++**Character target:** vintage barbershop; heavy lavender + coumarin + oakmoss with patchouli-vetiver base; warm-aromatic-mossy