no cap | OK |+| Vetiver EO | 0.80% | no cap | OK |+| Ambrox Super (active) | 0.48% | no cap | OK |+| Eugenol | 0.20% | 0.5% | OK |+| **Evernyl** | **0.08%** | **~0.10%** | **near ceiling โ€” measure precisely** |++### Why This Reads Like Drakkar Noir++- **Lavender at `2.40%` neat** โ€” twice V1, three times V2. This is *the* defining axis. The bottle smells of lavender first, everything else second.+- **Coumarin at `0.48%` neat** โ€” the highest in the set. Tonka-hay sweetness as a structural element, not as gourmand garnish.+- **Evernyl at `0.08%` (near IFRA ceiling)** โ€” real oakmoss-effect, the missing element of V1 and V2. This is what makes it read *classical* fougรจre.+- **Patchouli `0.80%` + Vetiver `0.80%`** โ€” earthy-mossy base that V1 and V2 don't touch. This is also part of the "vintage" character.+- **Ambrox at vintage-low `0.48%`** โ€” Drakkar Noir was a 1982 release; Ambroxan was not a category staple until the 2010s. The bottle should not project Ambrox-skin-warmth like V1.+- **No grapefruit, no lime, no pink pepper proxy at top.** Just bergamot + petitgrain + cardamom + eugenol โ€” classical 1980s masculine top notes.+- **No Sandalore reduction** โ€” sandalwood was central to 1980s masculine; it stays at `1.0%` neat alongside cedar.++### What V3 Teaches++The actual *original* fougรจre grammar โ€” lavender + coumarin + oakmoss + patchouli/vetiver. **This is the family at its purest.** Comparing V3 against V1 and V2 side-by-side teaches what the modern category drift looks like: 1982 โ’ 2015 is a story of moss disappearing, woods becoming abstract (Iso E), and Ambroxan replacing oakmoss as the base anchor.++### Safety Note On V3++Evernyl at `0.08%` is intentionally close to the IFRA Cat 4 ceiling (`~0.1%` finished product). Measure the `24 ยตL` precisely against a tared vial; do not estimate by drop count. If unsure, use `20 ยตL` instead โ€” `0.067%` is still enough for a clear moss read and gives a `30%` IFRA headroom buffer.++---++## Cross-Variation Comparison++| Axis | V1 Sauvage | V2 Bleu | V3 Drakkar |+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |+| Ambrox Super (neat % EDP) | 1.96% | 1.50% | 0.48% |+| Iso E Super (neat % EDP) | 2.40% | 4.00% | 1.60% |+| Lavender EO (neat % EDP) | 1.20% | 0.80% | 2.40% |+| Coumarin (neat % EDP) | 0.06% | 0.06% | 0.48% |+| Evernyl (neat % EDP) | 0% | 0% | 0.08% |+| Patchouli + Vetiver (neat % EDP) | 0% | 0.10% | 1.60% |+| Hedione (neat % EDP) | 1.20% | 1.60% | 1.20% |+| Total citrus top (neat % EDP) | 4.50% | 3.60% | 2.40% |+| Era / archetype | 2015+ modern | 2010+ modern | 1982 classical |+| Dominant character marker | Ambrox + pepper | Iso E + cedar | lavender + moss |++**The structural story across the three:**++- V3 (1982): the family lives on `lavender + coumarin + oakmoss + patchouli`. Ambrox is incidental. Citrus is supporting.+- V2 (2010s): oakmoss is gone (regulatory and fashion); Iso E Super becomes the architecture; Ambrox enters as moderate base.+- V1 (2015+): Ambrox dominates; lavender quiets; eugenol+cardamom replaces classical moss as the bite material.++This is why all three score as *aromatic fougรจre* under any reasonable family classifier despite radically different smell profiles. The family is more flexible than people think; what changes is *which axis carries the family signal*.++---++## Mixing Protocol (Common To All Three)++### 1. Prepare BHT antioxidant++Weigh `~1.2 mg` BHT into a clean 1 mL vial. Add `200 ยตL` ethanol 96%; swirl to dissolve. The `200 ยตL` of ethanol carrier counts as part of the concentrate volume.++### 2. Add to concentrate vial in base โ’ top order++Generally: lowest-VP base materials first (musks, Ambrox, Iso E, woods), then heart (Hedione, lavender, linalyl acetate), then top (citrus, petitgrain, beta-pinene). Specific orders are listed in each variation's table by tier label.++For V3 specifically: add `Evernyl` first (it is a crystalline solid that needs the longest dissolution time in ethanol).++### 3. Top up with ethanol 96%++After all materials are in, the concentrate vial should hold approximately `6,000 ยตL`. Verify by weight or by graduated transfer. If short, top up with ethanol 96%.++### 4. Bottle and macerate++Transfer concentrate to the 30 mL bottle. Add `24,000 ยตL` ethanol 96%. Cap, invert `20ร—` gently. **Macerate `4 weeks minimum`** before final evaluation.++The 4-week maceration is non-negotiable for fougรจres. Lavender + coumarin + Evernyl integration takes longer than oriental ambers because the aromatic-axis materials need to cross-condition with the woody base before the family read clarifies. Judging at 1 week is misleading.++### 5. Evaluation protocol++- **Day 7:** check direction only. Does the family read fougรจre?+- **Day 14:** check structure. Is the lavender-coumarin-base axis clear?+- **Day 28:** make the verdict. Is it the right archetype?+- **Day 60:** retest cold. Maceration is fully done by here.++---++## What To Do With This Set++1. **Pick one variation to make first.** The recommendation is **V1 (Sauvage)** โ€” it teaches the modern category and is the most wearable in Thai climate.+2. **Make all three eventually.** The educational value is in the *comparison*. Sniffing V1, V2, V3 side-by-side on Day 28 teaches more than making any single one.+3. **Do not modify the recipes during the first build.** The point is to build the archetype clean, then learn from the result. Modifications come on V2 of each, not V1.+4. **Compare against a real bottle on Day 28.** Buy a Sauvage 5 mL travel size or a Bleu de Chanel sampler. The reference comparison is what closes the educational loop.++The discipline lesson is the same across all three: **the materials you didn't add are as important as the materials you did**.diff --git a/formulas/collections/Mass_Market_Six_Families_2026-05-02.md b/formulas/collections/Mass_Market_Six_Families_2026-05-02.mdnew file mode 100644index 0000000..4b419dc--- /dev/null+++ b/formulas/collections/Mass_Market_Six_Families_2026-05-02.md@@ -0,0 +1,385 @@