3 % | 1.6 % | โ“ |+| Geraniol | Plum Velvet 0.27 % | 5.3 % | โ“ |+| Isoeugenol | not used | n/a | โ€” |+| Indole 10 % | Velvet Bloom 0.0027 % | not IFRA-restricted | โ“ |++**Action item:** reduce **Velvet Bloom** Cinnamaldehyde from 20 ยตL to 15 ยตL (0.05 %) before mixing โ€” the only IFRA edge in the collection.++---++## Why these specific sub-family choices++- **Floral โ’ Fruity Floral** rather than White Floral or Powdery: Fruity Floral has been the #1 women's-launch sub-family every year since 2010. (White Floral is more polarizing; Powdery is a niche-leaning sub-family in the 2020s mass market.)+- **Oriental โ’ Vanilla Amber** rather than Spicy Amber or Floral Amber: vanilla-gourmand orientals (Black Opium, La Vie est Belle, Good Girl) drive the bulk of women's amber-family revenue. Spicy Amber leans more masculine; Floral Amber is a smaller commercial slice.+- **Woody โ’ Aromatic Woody** rather than Sandalwood or Mossy Woody: Sauvage and Bleu de Chanel single-handedly anchor men's mass-market 2015โ€“2025. Sandalwood (Egoiste-style) is more niche-leaning today; Mossy Woody (Aramis-style) is heritage-only.+- **Chypre โ’ Fruity Chypre** rather than Floral Chypre or Green Chypre: post-2009 oakmoss restriction reset the chypre family โ€” Fruity Chypre (Coco Mademoiselle, Sรฌ) became the dominant modern chypre because the fruit + patchouli + Evernyl signature reads correctly to mass audiences without true oakmoss.+- **Fougรจre โ’ Aromatic Fougรจre** rather than Sweet Fougรจre or Fresh Fougรจre: the lavender + coumarin + woody-mossy aromatic fougรจre is the textbook men's mass-market structure (Cool Water, Brut, Drakkar Noir, Azzaro). Sweet Fougรจre (Pour Homme Intense) and Fresh/Aquatic Fougรจre are smaller sub-slices.+- **Fresh โ’ Aquatic** rather than Citrus or Green: Aquatic anchors the summer/unisex mass-market segment. Pure citrus (4711 cologne) is heritage-only; Green (Chanel No. 19 type) is much more niche-leaning today.diff --git a/formulas/collecti