the base. |+| 44 | Kephalis | 4 | **Transparent woody-amber anchor** โ€” ODT ~0.01 ppb โ’ enormous OAV at 4 ยตL. Adds a structural backbone to the base without introducing a new recognizable note. At 0.04% of concentrate, it operates below standalone perceptibility โ€” felt as structure, not smelled as "Kephalis." The woody-amber register aligns with the existing Iso E Super / Cedarwood base without competing. |+| 45 | Benzyl Benzoate | +80 | **Extended reservoir formation** โ€” Brings total to 360 ยตL. More fixative mass in a 50 mL ethanol volume means a slower evaporation curve, stretching the lavender heart from ~2 hr toward 3-4 hr. Near-odorless โ€” contributes character-free fixation. |+| 46 | Ambrettolide 10% | +200 | **Skin-hugging warmth** โ€” Brings total to 740 ยตL dilution (74 ยตL active). Ambrettolide has >300 hr tenacity and excellent skin substantivity โ€” it forms the deepest reservoir layer. The fruity-wine warmth adds skin-intimacy without competing with lavender. |+| 47 | Clary Sage EO | +30 | **Herbal-bridge reinforcement** โ€” Brings total to 130 ยตL. Compensates for the longer evaporation arc: as the base extends, the herbal bridge needs more mass to stay connected across the expanded timeline. |+| 48 | Heliotropal | +5 | **Powder tail extension** โ€” Brings total to 20 ยตL. Still under the family-shifting ceiling (โค22.5 ยตL for ~9 mL concentrate). Extends the almond-powder softness into the base alongside Terpinyl Acetate's herbal trail. |++**G subtotal: 439 ยตL** | **New materials: 1 (Kephalis)**++---++## Final Numbers โ€” 50 mL++| | ยตL | mL |+|---|----:|----:|+| Base concentrate (original) | 5,691 | 5.69 |+| Layer D (Ellena overlay) | 562 | 0.56 |+| Layer E (soliflore) | 2,294 | 2.29 |+| Layer F (hedonic) | 190 | 0.19 |+| Layer G (longevity) | 439 | 0.44 |+| **Total concentrate** | **9,176** | **9.18** |+| Ethanol 96% (to add) | 40,824 | 40.82 |+| **Total bottle** | **50,000** | **50.00** |+| **Concentration** | **18.4%** | **EdP** |++---++## What Changed โ€” Full Analysis++### Before (Malle Mod โ’ 30 mL)+The Ellena overlay added photorealistic stem and earth to the warm woody-musky base, but the formula was a **woody-aromatic with lavender** disguised as a lavender fragrance. The lavender sat on top of a massive Iso E Super + Hedione + Cedarwood + Coumarin structure that dominated the drydown. Aromatic, dry, angular โ€” interesting but not beautiful.++### After Layer E (Soliflore โ’ 50 mL)+Lavender established as the **dominant character across all evaporation phases** โ€” the linalool deficit was fixed, the camphoraceous gap was filled, and the herbal-bridge materials (Clary Sage, Rosemary, Bergamot) created a complete lavender plant illusion.++### After Layer G (Longevity Optimized โ’ 50 mL)+The lavender signature now persists through the deep drydown via Terpinyl Acetate + Kephalis structural anchoring:++| Phase | What you smell | Dominant materials |+|-------|---------------|-------------------|+| **Opening (0-15 min)** | Fresh-citrus lavender blast with jasmine sparkle, stem-green snap, ionone shimmer | Linalool (VP 15.8 Pa) + Beta-Pinene (VP 320 Pa) + Bergamot Sicilian + Hedione HC + Beta Ionone |+| **Heart (15 min-3 hr)** | Sweet-herbal lavender body wrapped in rose-plum richness and soft almond powder | Linalyl Acetate (VP 17.5 Pa) + Lavender EOs + Clary Sage + Damascenone + Heliotropal |+| **Late Heart (3-5 hr)** | Herbal-lavender echo, warm clary-ambery bridge, soft skin-musk intimacy | Terpinyl Acetate (VP 0.4 Pa) + Clary Sage + Ambrettolide + Benzyl Benzoate |+| **Base (5-8+ hr)** | Coumarinic-hay powder, transparent woody-amber structure, cool mineral trail | Terpinyl Acetate + Coumarin + Heliotropal + Kephalis + Romandolide + Ambrox |++### Hedonic Architecture++| Axis | Materials | Effect |+|------|-----------|--------|+| **Radiance** | Hedione (750) + Hedione HC (100) + Bergamot Sicilian (80) | Floral bloom + citrus sparkle โ€” the formula projects with brilliance |+| **Richness** | Damascenone (0.37 ยตL active) + Javanol (75) + Coumarin (48 active) | Dark-fruity depth + sandalwood intimacy + hay-sweet warmth |+| **Powder** | Heliotropal (20) + Beta Ionone (0.5 active) | Vintage-luxury softness โ€” transforms angular herbal into rounded elegance |+| **Clean musk** | Romandolide (540) + Ambrettolide (74 active) + Zenolide (135) | Transparent skin-cocoon โ€” projection + intimacy + freshness |+| **Structure** | Kephalis (4) + Iso E Super (780) + Terpinyl Acetate (245) + Benzyl Benzoate (360) | Transparent woody-amber anchor + herbal base persistence + evaporation gradient |++### Key Hedonic Material Roles++- **Damascenone (0.37 ยตL active):** The highest OAV-per-ยตL material in the formula. ODT 0.004 ppb means even sub-ยตL active creates perceptibility orders of magnitude above threshold. Adds the "dark expensive richness" dimension that makes a formula feel niche rather than functional. The rose facet sits *behind* lavender, not beside it.+- **Heliotropal (15 ยตL):** Vintage-powder signature. At 0.17% of concentrate, it's below its standalone impact threshold โ€” it adds texture (softness, roundness) rather than an identifiable "heliotrope note." Bridges lavender's herbal freshness to coumarin's hay-sweet base.+- **Hedione HC (100 ยตL):** The HC isomer has a cleaner, more transparent jasmine-radiance than standard Hedione. Adds sparkle to the top notes without the waxy-fatty body that standard Hedione develops. The combined Hedione system (850 ยตL total) is now the second-largest material group after lavender.+- **Beta Ionone (0.5 ยตL active):** ODT 0.007 ppb. At this dose, it creates a transparent violet-ionone powder that's felt as a shimmer rather than a note. Ionones have the unique ability to make entire compositions feel more diaphanous โ€” they "ionize" the air around the fragrance.+- **Terpinyl Acetate (245 ยตL):** The unsung hero of lavender longevity. VP 0.4 Pa means this is the only material in the formula that carries the herbal-lavender signature into the deep drydown (5-8+ hr). Without it, the lavender character dies at ~2 hr when linalyl acetate evaporates. The boost from 125 โ’ 245 ยตL extends the "lavender ghost" from a whisper to a clear trail.+- **Kephalis (4 ยตL):** Transparent structural anchor. At 0.04% of concentrate and ODT ~0.01 ppb, it operates as architecture rather than aroma โ€” felt as "the formula has a spine" rather than smelled as "Kephalis." Adds the missing base-note gravity without introducing a competing character.+- **Ambrettolide (74 ยตL active):** The deepest skin-reservoir layer. >300 hr tenacity means it's still there when everything else is gone. The fruity-wine warmth adds a skin-intimacy that makes the formula feel personal rather than projected. The boost from 54 โ’ 74 ยตL active deepens the reservoir without pushing the musk character forward.++### Odor Family+**Aromatic Lavender Soliflore** โ€” Unchanged. The hedonic materials serve as texture and finish, not as competing floral or oriental characters. Heliotropal at 15 ยตL is well below the family-shifting ceiling (โค21 ยตL equivalent).++### What Was Considered and Rejected โ€” Layer E++| Material | Why rejected |+|----------|-------------|+| More Lavender EO (Bontaux or HA) | Already at 1,680 ยตL. More EO adds complexity but doesn't fix the fundamental linalool deficit. Need molecular precision, not volume. |+| Juniper Berry EO | Would pull the aromatic register toward gin rather than lavender. Too coniferous-distinct. |+| Dihydromyrcenol | Would add a laundry-clean synthetic edge that undermines the photorealistic botanical character. |+| More Hedione | Already at 750 ยตL. Adding more would push the formula toward jasmine territory, competing with lavender for the dominant floral slot. |+| Cashmeran | Would introduce a textile-warmth dimension that shifts the drydown toward oriental. The base is already warm enough. |+| Clove / Eugenol | Would introduce spice competition. Lavender soliflore should be